{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward","id":720264,"title":"[Ex3] Lunars moving forward","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-23T12:57:39-07:00","id":720264,"title":"[Ex3] Lunars moving forward","content":"I like what the lunars have become from the description in Ex3 book. I love it! They're big! They're strong! They're <b>angry!</b><br /> <br /> Big difference is that they've removed the Solar bond. Not just removed it, but torn it free! Unsurprisingly the lunars do not want it back, and nor do I!<br /> <br /> However, the wrirteup left some things unsaid (as well it should not being the lunar book) and I'd like to take the opportunity to discuss them and the possibilities we now have. <br /> <br /> <b><u>First</u></b>, they're the shapshifting masters. Let's take that to the logical extreme. Why should a master of his or her own form be limited to only that of the animal they kill? Why can a lunar who has killed multiple individuals of a species not be able to mix and match traits from individuals? Why can't they add wings to a shape if they want? Oh wait, they totally can with the right knacks. Okay, why then can't they <i>remove </i>these features? Like from a wyld mutant form? or... from <i>their own</i> form? What I'm proposing is that the lunars were meant to be the perfect foil to the wyld and wyld-born threats from inception. When the gods were creating the chosen in the first place surely they knew that the wyld was a legitimate threat and that shape shifting or wyld-like attacks were a thing. It makes sense that they would plan for these sorts of threats with an exalt that deals with that stuff. So basically I'm saying that the <b>lunars should not need tattoos to be immune to wyld mutation and shaping.</b> This makes sense in game. Like I said before, the lunars are masters of modifying their own forms. It is absolutely inconceivable that the wyld can simply override that ability. therefore, make it so that the lunar can buy charms and knacks that make them immune to shaping stuff, or make it bend to their will. Someone tries to turn you into a statue? Surprise! Instead all you've done is give me an armored carapace! Or nothing happens! or I turn into a statue and back again, only this time angrier and with more power! The options are endless when you consider lunars as an exalt made to master the wyld and its energies rather than an exalt that's being poisoned by it and slowly going insane in mind and form. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Second</u></b>, moonsilver tattoos. What to do with them? They're a really cool thematic effect and I'd hate to lose them. On the other hand I'd <i>hate</i> to see them retain the 'get these or die' aspect that lunars have right now. Make moonsilver tattoos additive rather than mandatory! My first point feeds into this. If you allow lunars to build charms or knacks that allow them to be masters of the wyld and immune to the harmful effects of travelling it rather than building the protection into their skin, you make things a lot better. It also frees up the thematics of the tattoos for other stuff. Traditionally the tattoos fix the caste of the lunar in question and that makes a certain amount of sense. However, I'm not convinced we need this mechanic. If they don't have the tattoos they're at the mercy of the moon cycle rather than their own agency. I'd far prefer to have a changing caste as a viable, character driven option, but I'll talk about that in a bit. Moonsilver tattoos could be used as a silver pact power-boost type thing. If you have the silver pact as a faction focused on the destruction of the realm and the usurping dragon-blood and traitorous Sidereal then perhaps the moonsilver tattoos are primarily to <b>make a lunar more resistant to charms use</b>. Make the silver pact into a force that has reshaped themselves so that they can deal unrelenting destruction against other exalts! I envision the lunars as a little bit like Batman. You defeat him with surprise but if he has a chance to shape himself to the task then there will be no stopping him.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Third</u></b>, lunar castes and fixing them in place. I feel that the idea of a lunar trading between castes has a lot of merit. Being <i>forced</i> to change castes is not terribly good for an exalt with their own agency. However you can't just have a lunar change at will as that would certainly end up as game-breaking. I propose this: <b>by default the lunar caste is set by the dot total in their caste attributes/# of charms.</b> This allows a lunar to shift their focus over time while not being game breaking. Make a lunar choose a caste at character creation to represent their current aptitudes. If the player wants to shift caste they'd still have to buy non-caste charms and attributes at more expensive levels until they swap over to the new caste. Allows the lunar to be flexible. Hell, you could have a character ride on the raggety edge bewtween castes, but they'd be spending a ton more xp on keeping their non-caste stuff level with their caste stuff. In addition you could add in that moonsilver tattoos <i>do </i>fix your caste if you want the caste power while still specializing elsewhere. This even explains Ma-Ha-Suchi a bit. Perhaps he started as a changing moon caste all roses and charm and then ended up a full moon to reflect his nature after the usurpation. Lunars are the most flexible of the exalts after all.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Fourth</u></b>, Chimersim. Still kinda feels like a dirty word right? I don't think it has to be! What if, instead of being poisoned by the wyld, chimeras are what you get when you give a person unbelievable power and shapeshifting ability then exile him to the borders of reality, have everyone hunt him as a monster, has his entire family turn against him, and then add the realities of the unprepared wandering through the wyld. Most exalted would be able to deal with this. most wouldn't worry about it. But would they all? <b>In short, chimeras are lunar exalts who went mad</b> and simply realized that there really wasn't any limit to shapeshifting. They're something all lunars could be if they strove for it, but who in their right mind would want to? this fits with Ma-Ha-Suchi very well. Mr. goat-wolf himself simply went over the edge from the usurpation and everything else. Hell, his actions sure seem like those of a madman. This would create a rife storytelling opportunity as the threat of chimerism is still there, but it's not from the wyld. It's <b>you.</b> What would you do to avoid becoming a chimera? What would you stoop to to save your family? What would you do if you lost them anyway? Classic faustian type thing. great power at a cost of losing your humanity and ultimately your sanity. This has the upshot of never making a PC unplayable as well. After all, the Solars went mad in the first age. If the lunars went mad as well, what form would it take? I think this is a viable one. Imagine a lunar pushing their shapeshiting powers in an effort to transcend limits on them. Until the s<i>hape </i>part of shapeshifting gives way entirely to make room for the <i>shifting</i>.<br /> <br /> tl/dr: Lunars should be able to be masters of the wyld as exalted. IE They have charms that allow them to use the wyld energies for their benefit. Not Wyld-shaping, but rather wyld-using charms. Make Moonsilver tattoos a thing that the silver pact uses to make them more effective against exalted opponents rather than an absolute requirement for non-crazy lunars. Could be something else, but remove the mandatory aspect of them. Allow lunars to reshape themselves over time even up to the point of letting them shift their caste if they work towards it. Out of all exalts it makes sense for lunars to have this ability. Finally, make chimerism a function of a lunar simply giving in to insanity and letting go of their humanity and logic entirely to embrace pure chaos. There is no need for external forces to force a lunar to this point, it's far more chilling for it to be something that every lunar watches out for in themselves. <br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Anything here that would be utter crap? Anything I missed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T13:09:36-07:00","id":720306,"title":"","content":"You seem be unacquainted with a number of points made <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Presumably, they still stand.<br /> <br /> Forget everything about 2e, essentially. Let go of the Wyld influence in all of its forms, preconceptions over what a chimera is, and past characterizations. Presumably, Fury and its ilk won't be appearing as such, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T13:27:38-07:00","id":720373,"title":"","content":"We've been told that Chimera are now Lunars who've decided to evolve their Spirit Shape by adding the traits of other animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T13:32:30-07:00","id":720408,"title":"","content":"Thankfully, Lunars are no longer exiled to the boring lava lamp edges of the world, while all of the actual interesting stuff happens well a good distance within the edges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T13:40:24-07:00","id":720450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward#post720264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big difference is that they've removed the Solar bond. Not just removed it, but torn it free! Unsurprisingly the lunars do not want it back, and nor do I!</div> </div> </div> </div>It still exists. Not every Solar or Lunar is part of a bond, and it's not the one-way leash it was in previous editions - there are several mentions of &quot;Lunar Mates&quot; throughout the book, but the only one with mechanical impact is in Stubborn Boar Defense (which raises resolve against social influence if you resisted this influence once before)... which mentions that the Solar's Lunar Mate is never affected, so no added mental defenses against your mate. That's right, the one mechanical impact the Bond has so far is giving an advantage to the Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T13:51:40-07:00","id":720517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=720450#post720450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still exists. Not every Solar or Lunar is part of a bond, and it's not the one-way leash it was in previous editions - there are several mentions of &quot;Lunar Mates&quot; throughout the book, but the only one with mechanical impact is in Stubborn Boar Defense (which raises resolve against social influence if you resisted this influence once before)... which mentions that the Solar's Lunar Mate is never affected, so no added mental defenses against your mate. That's right, the one mechanical impact the Bond has so far is giving an advantage to the Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost undoubtedly it's going to resemble the setup from 1e, when taking on bonds between an indivudal Lunar and an individual Solar was strictly voluntary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:15:33-07:00","id":720719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=720306#post720306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem be unacquainted with a number of points made <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Presumably, they still stand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the link! Been a long time since I've been on the forums (my username was deleted forever due to inactivity it seems). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=720306#post720306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forget everything about 2e, essentially. Let go of the Wyld influence in all of its forms, preconceptions over what a chimera is, and past characterizations. Presumably, Fury and its ilk won't be appearing as such, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgetting everything about 2E would be a crying shame. there was some bloody good stuff in there! You'll note that in my points, the wyld has no influence on lunars. To the point where they are better able to deal with it than any other exalt type. <i>By celestial design.</i> The only influence I indicated the wyld may have on them is if they spend too much time alone in crazy land they may end up crazy themselves.<br /> <br /> also my version of chimerism seems to follow fairly closely with what the authors have talked about. Adding other animal bits to your war form but taken to the extreme. <br /> <br /> Besides, I started this thread to give us some ways of doing lunars <b>now</b>. So far all we've got is the exalt writeup in Ex3 which is still pretty cool but only scratches the surface. And that's all we're really gonna have until we sink our teeth into the lunar splat book unfortunately","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:22:52-07:00","id":720738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=720450#post720450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still exists. Not every Solar or Lunar is part of a bond, and it's not the one-way leash it was in previous editions - there are several mentions of &quot;Lunar Mates&quot; throughout the book, but the only one with mechanical impact is in Stubborn Boar Defense (which raises resolve against social influence if you resisted this influence once before)... which mentions that the Solar's Lunar Mate is never affected, so no added mental defenses against your mate. That's right, the one mechanical impact the Bond has so far is giving an advantage to the Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the writeup in Ex3 it seems that the bond was entirely shattered. There might be isolated exceptions, the same way there was a handful of solars who escaped the jade prison but otherwise the bond is gone. Hell, from the lunar writeup it <i>was</i> the mind-controlling version of the bond as in previous editions. It specifically calls the lunars slaves of the solars. There seems to be something that <i>may </i>replace the bond but it certainly won't look like what we've seen before. I also agree that it will likely be voluntary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:29:31-07:00","id":720779,"title":"","content":"All I really know or care about 3e Lunars is that they damn well better have a Charm called Meerkat Steals the Spotlight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":338,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","user":"Coik","date":". 10-23-2015, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T16:58:18-07:00","id":721130,"title":"","content":"3e Lunars appear to be a new, more reasonable incarnation of te 1e Lunars. I'm not too sure what to think of the info we got.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact's focus on destroying the Realm through slow erosion of its resources is epic alright, but the guys need something more construtive to do. We already have Abyssals for spreading death and entropy and the whole destroying the chains of the past thing reminds me a bit too much of the 2e Neverborn, but that could be just me.<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder if they'll have something they'll be the best at this time around?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:06:23-07:00","id":721304,"title":"","content":"Lunars, we have been told, are better at something than the other Exalted - shapeshifting into animals. And one look in that section of the antagonists chapter should rightly have people shitting their pants in fear at this detail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=720719#post720719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the link! Been a long time since I've been on the forums (my username was deleted forever due to inactivity it seems).</div> </div> </div> </div>Harsh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Forgetting everything about 2E would be a crying shame. there was some bloody good stuff in there! </div> </div> </div>Such as?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'll note that in my points, the wyld has no influence on lunars. To the point where they are better able to deal with it than any other exalt type. <i>By celestial design.</i> The only influence I indicated the wyld may have on them is if they spend too much time alone in crazy land they may end up crazy themselves. </div> </div> </div>Still out of place. Lunars aren't the Wyld Exalted. It's doubtful that any kind of Exalted is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also my version of chimerism seems to follow fairly closely with what the authors have talked about. Adding other animal bits to your war form but taken to the extreme. </div> </div> </div>It didn't quite seem like it? Chimerism as proposed is just going to be a matter of having heavy symbolic importance to two or more animals instead of just having a single totem. It's like 2e's Perfected Hybrid Interaction, only more limited in available features and not looked upon as a step toward madness. No one's going to think that you're going mad, and you don't have to go mad in order to be a chimera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, I started this thread to give us some ways of doing lunars <b>now</b>. So far all we've got is the exalt writeup in Ex3 which is still pretty cool but only scratches the surface. And that's all we're really gonna have until we sink our teeth into the lunar splat book unfortunately </div> </div> </div>Well, for starters, I'd guess that the elders get their dignity back and stop being nearly so edgy. No more Rutting Pens, no more society built around vindictively beating up Dragon-Blooded in an oddly well-preserved marine arcology, no more being a secret master of the Delzahn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:32:26-07:00","id":721373,"title":"","content":"I like the way they've changed the Tell in 3rd ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:36:18-07:00","id":721383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=721373#post721373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the way they've changed the Tell in 3rd ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah they changed the Tell mechanic to how it always should have been, a &quot;spot this!&quot; mechanic, rather than trying to get cute with Social mechanics and just making it dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 10-23-2015, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T19:09:26-07:00","id":721422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=721373#post721373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the way they've changed the Tell in 3rd ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did they do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T19:10:42-07:00","id":721424,"title":"","content":"Also, if you're playing Red Jaws, when you're walking around in human form people don't for some reason not notice the fact you have one eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T20:22:25-07:00","id":721593,"title":"","content":"I also note that turning back into human form is a free, reflexive action, but turning into your totem form is not. So having a Tyrant Lizard totem doesn't let you reflexively turn into a Tyrant Lizard.<br /> <br /> I hope this means people will choose animals for totem forms they think are cool, rather than which one is mechanically best.<br /> <br /> I also note that turning into an animal gives you their dice pool, not their attributes. Is that a placeholder, or how it will work eventually? All the animals in the book don't have attributes listed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T20:29:15-07:00","id":721602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=721130#post721130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e Lunars appear to be a new, more reasonable incarnation of te 1e Lunars. I'm not too sure what to think of the info we got.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact's focus on destroying the Realm through slow erosion of its resources is epic alright, but the guys need something more construtive to do. We already have Abyssals for spreading death and entropy and the whole destroying the chains of the past thing reminds me a bit too much of the 2e Neverborn, but that could be just me.<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder if they'll have something they'll be the best at this time around?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure that when they get more then a few pages of focus they will be fleshed out and shown to have Lunars interested in something besides smashing the Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=721422#post721422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did they do?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is back to not having to be an animal trait, Ma-Ha-Suchi once again speaks with a voice that sounds like silver bells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:04:30-07:00","id":721703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=721593#post721593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope this means people will choose animals for totem forms they think are cool, rather than which one is mechanically best.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what if the animal I think is cool <i>is </i>a Tyrant Lizard or otherwise &quot;Mechanically best&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:07:55-07:00","id":721707,"title":"","content":"Then they can still choose it.<br /> <br /> It's just that the game doesn't punish players for choosing a cat rather than a tyrant lizard. Or, for that matter, a bird over a tyrant lizard (having a small bird at 1 mote instead of 3 motes is very useful for spying in 2e, even if it lacks the excellency-punching powers of a tyrant lizard totem).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T22:41:56-07:00","id":721917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=720738#post720738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the writeup in Ex3 it seems that the bond was entirely shattered. There might be isolated exceptions, the same way there was a handful of solars who escaped the jade prison but otherwise the bond is gone. Hell, from the lunar writeup it <i>was</i> the mind-controlling version of the bond as in previous editions. It specifically calls the lunars slaves of the solars. There seems to be something that <i>may </i>replace the bond but it certainly won't look like what we've seen before. I also agree that it will likely be voluntary.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does mention the bond's destruction, but I wouldn't make bets yet on whether it was a complete destruction for every bond, or whether the bond was just unavailable during the Solar's absence and is now severely weakened (to the point of non-existence for many, but not all of them) as they return. Mostly because, whenever I asked a question about this to the devs, the answer was &quot;the Lunar book is waaaay of, and anything we say now may be changed till then&quot;, so even they don't seem to be sure - the comic seems to imply that &quot;bond carrying over from previous Exaltations&quot; is still an option.<br /> <br /> Also, where does it call them slaves? Sure, it mentions that they used to define themselves as the Solar's shadows (Silver Solar joke here?), but that's just a reference to the &quot;unbroken castes&quot;, which mirrored the Solar castes. It also mentions them as having been created as &quot;the Solar's seconds&quot;, but &quot;second in command&quot; is not &quot;slave&quot;. Otherwise, Luna herself would be TUC's slave.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":7262,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","user":"Amakawa Yuuto","date":". 10-24-2015, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T22:58:10-07:00","id":721931,"title":"","content":"I hope the Solar bond isn't completely going way.<br /> <br /> Pearl and Rose have renewed my interest in tragic and one-sided romances that end in nothing but heartbreak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T05:16:55-07:00","id":722646,"title":"","content":"For such a controversial thing, I would have thought the easiest thing would just to make it optional. So some Lunars have it and some don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T08:24:40-07:00","id":723125,"title":"","content":"I think that what struck me most about the Lunars this time around is how both Lunars and Luna are defined as &quot;iconoclasts.&quot; Now, being fascinated by history as I am, I only recognized this word in the context of the ancient Christian movement/heresy that held that icons should be removed, but I discovered that it also means those who hold against popular opinions.<br /> <br /> What implications this has for Lunars can be quite intriguing - I mean, there's the obvious, that the Lunars are <i>very much against</i> the current regime of Creation and of its Sidereal puppet masters, but looking more closely, I think I can see signs of Lunars playing the role of &quot;the other&quot; even with Solars. I mean, Stubborn Boar Defense, as has already been noted, allows a Lunar mate to slip past its defense. Imagine, now, that a Solar may be taking actions his or her Lunar disagrees with - the Lunar can keep harrying the Solar, continue bringing up the issue, and the Solar cannot just use the charm to disregard it. If what I'm getting from the implications of this is correct, the idea that the Lunars counterbalance the Solars even if they are working towards the same goals may be in what is coming in 3e. I <i>like</i> this.<br /> <br /> The other major thing that struck me about Lunars is very first sentence of their description page: &quot;The Chosen of the moon were forged in the chains of bondage but Luna only chooses those<br /> with the power to free themselves.&quot; It goes on to talk about how they are caught in the fangs of the past, and until they escape it, they have no freedom. I understand that there have been some concerns about how Lunars are so totally unsympathetic now, given what we have seen of them thus far, but I think these lines sort of hint at why they <i>are</i> sympathetic - they are traumatized, collectively (and individually, most likely), but as Chosen of Luna, they have the power to move past that trauma and become free of the past... which I think they're kind of failing to do, collectively, at the moment, but that's beside the point.<br /> <br /> I may be mistaken in my reading of these things, but what I see of the Lunars makes me very happy indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T09:32:41-07:00","id":723349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=721424#post721424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you're playing Red Jaws, when you're walking around in human form people don't for some reason not notice the fact you have one eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the same token, when a cat-eyed Lunar takes a cat form, no one notices that the cat has cat-eyes.<br /> <br /> They MIGHT notice that the cat has the exact same cat-eyes that they saw on that nice fellow earlier that morning... if they're suspicious enough to check a cat for a disguise and if they actually met the Lunar that morning. (Or REMEMBER the meeting, because the Lunar might have blanked out the memory.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T09:40:59-07:00","id":723376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=721424#post721424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you're playing Red Jaws, when you're walking around in human form people don't for some reason not notice the fact you have one eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? I didn't think that was his Tell since &quot;scratched out eye&quot; is hardly a specific animal trait :P<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T09:59:42-07:00","id":723427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=721130#post721130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e Lunars appear to be a new, more reasonable incarnation of te 1e Lunars. I'm not too sure what to think of the info we got.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact's focus on destroying the Realm through slow erosion of its resources is epic alright, but the guys need something more construtive to do. We already have Abyssals for spreading death and entropy and the whole destroying the chains of the past thing reminds me a bit too much of the 2e Neverborn, but that could be just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is <i>super</i> not just you. I started on 2e and found that edition's Lunars very interesting once you filtered out the bad attempts at Solar Heat, so the reversion you've noted... <i>worries</i> me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T10:01:33-07:00","id":723431,"title":"","content":"I feel like 3e Lunars' use of barbarian tribes as guided missiles they raise, radicalize, send at the Realm, and move on, is quite a bit more...rational and likely than the derpy 2e &quot;humans can stand on their own merits without Exalted, plz ignore all other setting supernaturals tho!&quot; TSR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 10-24-2015, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T10:25:35-07:00","id":723531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=723376#post723376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? I didn't think that was his Tell since &quot;scratched out eye&quot; is hardly a specific animal trait :P</div> </div> </div> </div>SoE lists it as wolf ears, so I think that Sunder meant that now it's back to being his eye, in an Odin-like way where people ignore that he has it and do stupid shit around him while he's disguised in a fit of dramatic irony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T10:52:04-07:00","id":723623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=723431#post723431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like 3e Lunars' use of barbarian tribes as guided missiles they raise, radicalize, send at the Realm, and move on, is quite a bit more...rational and likely than the derpy 2e &quot;humans can stand on their own merits without Exalted, plz ignore all other setting supernaturals tho!&quot; TSR.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't deny that the Thousand Streams' details were in need of work, or that this execution makes more sense than that one. It's a moral one-eighty, though, and I am not okay with <i>that.</i><br /> <br /> It's like if we were still being told that the <i>only</i> things for Sidereals to do was Hunt Solars and that that dominated all they had become in the modern age. It's not just limiting, it's limiting to playing, at best, someone well-intentioned but horrifically destructive, and more likely an outright villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","user":"Valles","date":". 10-24-2015, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T13:06:08-07:00","id":724041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=723623#post723623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't deny that the Thousand Streams' details were in need of work, or that this execution makes more sense than that one. It's a moral one-eighty, though, and I am not okay with <i>that.</i><br /> <br /> It's like if we were still being told that the <i>only</i> things for Sidereals to do was Hunt Solars and that that dominated all they had become in the modern age. It's not just limiting, it's limiting to playing, at best, someone well-intentioned but horrifically destructive, and more likely an outright villain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, you're just not involved in that project...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T13:19:31-07:00","id":724058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=723623#post723623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't deny that the Thousand Streams' details were in need of work, or that this execution makes more sense than that one. It's a moral one-eighty, though, and I am not okay with <i>that.</i><br /> <br /> It's like if we were still being told that the <i>only</i> things for Sidereals to do was Hunt Solars and that that dominated all they had become in the modern age. It's not just limiting, it's limiting to playing, at best, someone well-intentioned but horrifically destructive, and more likely an outright villain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couple things.<br /> <br /> 1. I don't think that's described as something ALL Lunars do, or that all Lunars go about it in the extreme realpolitik way I described. Certainly some do, but other Lunars probably go about their goals in other ways. The Silver Pact is not the monolith of the Bureau of Destiny, and making it less like the Garou Nation is great for all the reasons that making it the Garou Nation to begin with didn't make sense. <br /> 2. I'm not sure I see the problem with a moral 180 when the past portrayal was not just derpy, but actively immersion-breakingly stupid.<br /> 3. I'm not sure the about face as to &quot;what are Lunars, as a whole, trying to do&quot; being centered on &quot;destroy the Realm&quot; is bad in light of having no solid focus in past eds except &quot;something something barbarians something fighting fair folk something forced breeding beastman army&quot;<br /> 4. In a way I like the solid greying of morality in the Realm vs Lunar war thing. Lunars are not just some ancient good guys who the current government won't leave alone; they're doing terrible things to support their goals, <i>which is a strategy that human beings employ and always have employed.</i><br /> <br /> Why was their 2e &quot;morality,&quot; which to me seemed to be &quot;farcically ignore the actual state of Creation to stick our heads in the sand re mortal societies that will not be able to last without us,&quot; a better state?<br /> <br /> I mean, is this the true ideal version of the Lunar narrative. I dunno. Probably not? I'm really not sure, because we never have had a good alternative to compare it to. We can't look at it like Yozis and say &quot;I prefer the GoD portrayal to the MOEP Infernals and CoCD Malfeas one,&quot; because 1e Lunars was an example of total bedshitting and 2e Lunars was narratively incoherent. I'm not sure TAW even answered the narrative question, so much as its goal was to make the mechanics not &quot;Solar Charms, but overcosted and silver-colored.&quot; <br /> <br /> Are they now filling a niche that was unfilled, and better than the sloppy lack of direction, set on the boring edges of the world, that they had as a splat in the past? I say absolutely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T13:28:26-07:00","id":724068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=723125#post723125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that what struck me most about the Lunars this time around is how both Lunars and Luna are defined as &quot;iconoclasts.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not actually new, that came up in Second Edition.<br /> <br /> I still don't like it, because it would mean that Lunars would always be defining themselves in opposition to something stronger than them, which would either prevent them from ever being a part of the dominant side of the equation or else leave them confused and directionless should they ever become the dominant power. Like the Ebon Dragon of Second Edition, they would lose all personal identity and become shallow and reactionary. A rebel always looking for a cause, any cause, every cause, just 'cause.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other major thing that struck me about Lunars is very first sentence of their description page: &quot;The Chosen of the moon were forged in the chains of bondage but Luna only chooses those with the power to free themselves.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Now THIS has me excited.<br /> <br /> Out of many attempts to find a &quot;shared narrative&quot; for the Lunar Exalted which wasn't just &quot;like the Solar Exalted, but silver&quot; and which was thematically-specific such as enjoyed by every non-Solar Exalted Host, few have been as powerful and appropriate as this:<br /> <br /> &quot;I was once a slave -- to my owner, to my passions, to my debt, to my culture, to my parents, to my ancestor ghost, to my god, to my delusions of grandeur -- until I choose to break free and escape -- to flee by the cover of night, to join a monastery, to declare bankruptcy and accept my jail sentence, to marry Juliet, to salt the ghoul's grave-shrine, to eat the god's sacrifice for myself, to accept that I was worthless...<br /> <br /> &quot;And in midst of casting off my chains, the Moon gave me Exaltation, so that the freedom I had grasped for would not end immediately in the face of the consequences.<br /> <br /> &quot;But as I grow into my power, I begin to feel the chains of a forgotten past trying to tie me down once more. If I am to truly attain the freedom promised to me, I must continue to destroy every fetter that everyone ever attempts to impose upon me.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 10-24-2015, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T13:46:20-07:00","id":724092,"title":"","content":"I liked the Thousand Streams River when I first saw it, but after thinking about it some more, I no longer do. Because what it really does is take the few accomplishments mortals actually have in the pre-3e setting (3e does seem to be treat them more seriously, but I haven't had time to dig into it yet) and give them to Lunars. Like, all those strong, independent and unique mortal cultures that stand on their own despite the presence of Exalted, gods and other divine personages? Joke's on you, kids, that's all Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T13:57:10-07:00","id":724104,"title":"","content":"I admit the hints at new lunars make me really wary, especially that emphasis on Rage. I don't want lunars to be more like WoD werewolves. And having something where &quot;all of this caste has this personality trait&quot; (e.g. all angry) is a roleplaying cardinal sin, in my book.<br /> Hopefully, my concerns are groundless. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2259-auroradragonkaya","name":"auroradragonkaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2259_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T14:32:08-07:00","id":724155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724068#post724068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not actually new, that came up in Second Edition.<br /> <br /> I still don't like it, because it would mean that Lunars would always be defining themselves in opposition to something stronger than them, which would either prevent them from ever being a part of the dominant side of the equation or else leave them confused and directionless should they ever become the dominant power. Like the Ebon Dragon of Second Edition, they would lose all personal identity and become shallow and reactionary. A rebel always looking for a cause, any cause, every cause, just 'cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is something to what you're saying here, I think, but I'm not sure that I agree with your conclusion. Iconoclasts do not need to be rebels - just to be in disagreement with how things <i>are</i>. That is to say, as in the example I made with the Stubborn Boar Defense, a Lunar who genuinely loves his or her Solar mate, or even just one who happens to feel that he or she can use them in a way that is beneficial to Creation might try to challenge that Solar to see things from multiple perspectives. I guess that to me, Lunars might be the counterbalance to an authority that all too often thinks <i>it</i> has the right answers. This doesn't mean that they don't fall prey to that tendency themselves, of course - witness the weaponization of cultures, the immense death-spiral that the Pact is contributing to - but that this is something that may well characterize Lunar behaviors and/or design choices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724068#post724068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now THIS has me excited.<br /> <br /> Out of many attempts to find a &quot;shared narrative&quot; for the Lunar Exalted which wasn't just &quot;like the Solar Exalted, but silver&quot; and which was thematically-specific such as enjoyed by every non-Solar Exalted Host, few have been as powerful and appropriate as this:<br /> <br /> &quot;I was once a slave -- to my owner, to my passions, to my debt, to my culture, to my parents, to my ancestor ghost, to my god, to my delusions of grandeur -- until I choose to break free and escape -- to flee by the cover of night, to join a monastery, to declare bankruptcy and accept my jail sentence, to marry Juliet, to salt the ghoul's grave-shrine, to eat the god's sacrifice for myself, to accept that I was worthless...<br /> <br /> &quot;And in midst of casting off my chains, the Moon gave me Exaltation, so that the freedom I had grasped for would not end immediately in the face of the consequences.<br /> <br /> &quot;But as I grow into my power, I begin to feel the chains of a forgotten past trying to tie me down once more. If I am to truly attain the freedom promised to me, I must continue to destroy ever fetter that everyone ever attempts to impose upon me.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with you here. To my eyes, the Lunars appear to be about the journey <i>even more</i> than the destination in a way Solars, for instance, aren't. It's about the search, not the ultimate discovery, because to Lunars, there <i>is</i> no ultimate discovery, only a continuing growth and change as a person. This doesn't mean constant random change, of course, but simply that Lunars, like Luna, change throughout their existence.<br /> <br /> EDIT: While yeah, all characters should grow and change in time, Lunars are <i>characterized</i> by this search for themselves and their rightful place, at least from what I've seen and am guessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":7858,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","user":"*End","date":".  Clarification 10-24-2015, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T14:42:21-07:00","id":724167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>auroradragonkaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724104#post724104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit the hints at new lunars make me really wary, especially that emphasis on Rage. I don't want lunars to be more like WoD werewolves. And having something where &quot;all of this caste has this personality trait&quot; (e.g. all angry) is a roleplaying cardinal sin, in my book.<br /> Hopefully, my concerns are groundless. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think they probably are. I honestly don't see the emphasis on rage that others do, but that's because I'm probably looking at it in a rather unique way. Rather than rage, I characterize what the Lunars are experiencing as loss, or seeking, or something like that. Think about it this way - the Lunars apparently lost <i>something</i> when the Solars vanished, and it may have been more than simply emotional (in that some magical connection existed between the Solars and Lunars). Since then, the elders who lived in the First Age have slowly been decreasing in number, but they still recall what it was to live in a world so much better than the Second Age, to live in a place where they weren't hunted like animals. From this arises their anger.<br /> <br /> The majority of the Lunars are probably not quite so emotionally invested in dethroning the Realm... except inasmuch as the Realm has basically demonized them, kicked them out of their homes, and probably tried to kill them many times over. When everything you've known has been taken from you, and suddenly there's a Silver Pact Lunar talking about how the evil Realm is awful and needs to fall, telling you about the age-old truth that you are, in fact, Chosen, and of a far greater sort than the Dragon-blooded who you have always been taught are the Princes of Earth, you may find yourself grasping this direction, because you need that direction...<br /> <br /> Then, as you carry out your actions, you may find yourself questioning why you are doing this rather than something else - this is what I see as the fangs of the past, still clinging to your Lunar, and freedom shall not be yours until you realize how to free yourself from them. But you can do so, because of who you are - that is why Luna Chose you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T15:23:44-07:00","id":724265,"title":"","content":"I think rage and anger are far broader, deeper and multi-dimensional as feelings, traits and motivations than people give them credit for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T15:51:10-07:00","id":724308,"title":"","content":"About the &quot;Tear Down the Realm&quot; thing? Yeah, that's what the Silver Pact does. That is its focus. And while I'm not sure if it was mentioned in the same paragraph or the one after it, it directly mentions that no, not all Lunars join into that plan. And those who don't join in aren't outcastes - they're just doing their own thing, and only help out in the Silver Pact's wars as part of favour trading. Or maybe because a friend asked them, or whatever. And in turn, the Silver Pact Lunars will do stuff that has nothing to do with tearing down the Realm, as part of their half of favour trading, helping out friends, or whatever.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T15:54:07-07:00","id":724310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724265#post724265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think rage and anger are far broader, deeper and multi-dimensional as feelings, traits and motivations than people give them credit for.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still highly limiting, and doesn't fit for every character.<br /> Heck, it doesn't really fit the personality of the Lunar who's going to be making a brief appearance in the Novia novel, so it will be interesting to see how that plays out. (Then again, it might just be a throwaway sentence and not really have any result at all, lol)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2259-auroradragonkaya","name":"auroradragonkaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2259_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T16:10:08-07:00","id":724326,"title":"","content":"If Lunars, as a group, are driven and partially defined by anger over the injustices done to them, and the state of Creation, it doesn't mean that every single Lunar is angry all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T16:11:44-07:00","id":724330,"title":"","content":"My impression: The <i>elder</i> Lunars have an agenda, based on the most traumatic event of their lives. They will reward you if you help them further this agenda, in part on the theory that you will slowly become what you do. If you just walk off, hey, they'll tell you that's cool, go do what you like . . . in the expectation that at some point, the Realm is gonna come after you for being Anathema anyway. The elders will make their pitch again when you're both angry with the Realm and needing a favor from the Silver Pact.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T16:35:44-07:00","id":724409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724330#post724330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression: The <i>elder</i> Lunars have an agenda, based on the most traumatic event of their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really my impression, at least not completely.<br /> The anger and rage seems to be their version of Essence Fever (... page 35-36). For Solars, the Essence Fever is to strive for glory, to impose their will onto the world. They're always driven to be more than they are, but quickly learn to control this. It explicitly mentions that the different types of Exalts have different Essence Fevers, and the stubborn rage of Lunars sounds similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T16:36:38-07:00","id":724411,"title":"","content":"With the Lunars' 3e tactic of raising up barbarian nations to assault the Realm in full knowledge they'll probably be wiped out in reprisal, it does to me seem like that is trying to play up a contrast between the Solars as the genuine &quot;freedom fighters&quot; and saviors vs the Lunars as seeming saviors who are actually at base inept at actually offering real succor, growth and hope to the Threshold and are really an exploitative, endless War of Attrition terrorist network. And I kind of don't think that's cool, or so interesting, really, although good writing may make it so.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I'm being very cynical though, and that's just me, and what I find interesting and don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T16:51:31-07:00","id":724478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724411#post724411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Lunars' 3e tactic of raising up barbarian nations to assault the Realm in full knowledge they'll probably be wiped out in reprisal, it does to me seem like that is trying to play up a contrast between the Solars as the genuine &quot;freedom fighters&quot; and saviors vs the Lunars as seeming saviors who are actually at base inept at actually offering real succor, growth and hope to the Threshold and are really an exploitative, endless War of Attrition terrorist network. And I kind of don't think that's cool, or so interesting, really, although good writing may make it so.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I'm being very cynical though, and that's just me, and what I find interesting and don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not being a backer, I haven't been able to read the pdf. But the impressions of my friends who have it are... NOT really positive towards new Lunars. At all. comparisons to 1E Lunars were drawn, and that honestly made me extremely queasy, because 1E Lunars were a shit sandwich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T16:56:02-07:00","id":724486,"title":"","content":"About the &quot;Raising up barbarian hordes to fight the realm, even though they're going to be wiped out&quot;...<br /> ...Those barbarians they recruit? They live right at the edge of Realm territory. It even calls out that Lunars rarely have to lie for their propaganda - these barbarians often are driven away and hunted by the realm.<br /> It's not a stretch to assume that many of these tribes are not just displaced, but actually driven into a corner and faced with extinction anyway. The Lunars help them put on one last fight. They don't <i>sell</i> it as such, but that's what they do. Instead of a slow and steady decline until their tribe just vanishes, the Lunars raise them up and allow them to go out in a blaze of glory.<br /> <br /> It's still based on selfish intentions, but that doesn't mean it has to be so entirely, especially when accounting for the fact that a lunar living long enough can see this &quot;slow and steady decline&quot; happening again and again. If they're going to vanish anyway, why not allow them to cause some damage to those who pushed them into this decline?<br /> <br /> <br /> (Not saying that this is the standard. There may be Lunars who are outright recruiting perfectly stable societies to wage a war against the realm. There may also be Lunars actually trying to save their tribes. The average is probably in between.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T17:02:38-07:00","id":724504,"title":"","content":"Mmm...who's to say the Solars won't do the same thing?<br /> <br /> Not as an action of unified policy like the Silver Pact, but some of them...it's an effective method.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T17:20:44-07:00","id":724557,"title":"","content":"I mostly feel like it's implied that they won't, as opposed to being genuine champions and protectors of nations who will die trying to protect their people, and that the readers and players are meant to draw that implicit comparison (which to me is not so much an interesting comparison, which I won't repeat). Who knows though? Mirror Flag certainly would. Yurgen Kaneko would balk at it I think, even if he might send his people and others to their death for &quot;authentic&quot; reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T17:24:04-07:00","id":724562,"title":"","content":"I find 3E lunars to be delightfully anarchistic. <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/0e/02/f5/0e02f53935d77e11a98c226e3861bc3c.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T17:34:51-07:00","id":724575,"title":"","content":"I think for Solars it will be more about context than institutional policy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T18:42:18-07:00","id":724711,"title":"","content":"Just as long as I can play a lunar who says &quot;fuck all that noise&quot; and spend his time playing around with his new powers and hunting dangerous and exotic creatures to test his superhuman attributes against and/or steel the shapes of,I'll be happy.<br /> <br /> The &quot;You can do as you want.&quot; things people have been saying are encouraging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T18:44:52-07:00","id":724713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724711#post724711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as long as I can play a lunar who says &quot;fuck all that noise&quot; and spend his time playing around with his new powers and hunting dangerous and exotic creatures to test his superhuman attributes against and/or steel the shapes of,I'll be happy.<br /> <br /> The &quot;You can do as you want.&quot; things people have been saying are encouraging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Holden said, it's pretty hard to to impose your monolithic agenda and authority on a dude who can turn into a bird and fly three thousand miles away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T18:55:15-07:00","id":724727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724713#post724713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Holden said, it's pretty hard to to impose your monolithic agenda and authority on a dude who can turn into a bird and fly three thousand miles away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's only half the potential issues preventing such a character motivation from being potentially rewarding, but it is very encouraging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T19:06:37-07:00","id":724737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724478#post724478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not being a backer, I haven't been able to read the pdf. But the impressions of my friends who have it are... NOT really positive towards new Lunars. At all. comparisons to 1E Lunars were drawn, and that honestly made me extremely queasy, because 1E Lunars were a shit sandwich.</div> </div> </div> </div>They should try to read Game of Thrones as at least one example some time. Because the bits of 3e Lunars I've read don't read like 1e Lunars at all. No sections on how you should be out raping at whatnot and barbarian life is THE SHIT because RAWR!,etc,etc and all the rest of the bad stuff.(edit note:If it sounds like I'm trying to sound light on the issues of 1e, I'm not. I don't remember how many years it's been since that hardcover came out but that shit still irritates me, and I don't even like Lunars) Do some Lunars effectively use entire societies of people in ruthlessly pragmatic attempts to erode the power and resources of the Realm? You bet. Is this substantially different from the rest of the brutal existences of a pseudo ancient world, world culture that makes up Creation? No. It's gritty and rather brutal setting of horrors and wonders for the average mortal in Creation. So while I recognize that what some of the Lunars are doing in the lens of a lot of in game moralities is rather rough, that isn't the same thing as the poor and hamfisted to outright disturbing bits that we got in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-24-2015, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T19:21:29-07:00","id":724755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724737#post724737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They should try to read Game of Thrones as at least one example some time. Because the bits of 3e Lunars I've read don't read like 1e Lunars at all. No sections on how you should be out raping at whatnot and barbarian life is THE SHIT because RAWR!,etc,etc and all the rest of the bad stuff.(edit note:If it sounds like I'm trying to sound light on the issues of 1e, I'm not. I don't remember how many years it's been since that hardcover came out but that shit still irritates me, and I don't even like Lunars) Do some Lunars effectively use entire societies of people in ruthlessly pragmatic attempts to erode the power and resources of the Realm? You bet. Is this substantially different from the rest of the brutal existences of a pseudo ancient world world culture that makes up Creation? No. It's gritty and rather brutal setting of horrors and wonders for the average mortal in Creation. So while I recognize that what some of the Lunars are doing in the lens of a lot of in game moralities is rather rough, that isn't the same thing as the poor and hamfisted to outright disturbing bits that we got in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>You were supposed to sympathize with First Edition Silver Pact <i>and </i>take it seriously. (That didn't work, but it was the intent.)<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact of Third Edition is very different. You CAN take them seriously, but you're not supposed to sympathize with what they're doing. Just like the Scarlet Dynasty, or the Sidereal Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T19:32:41-07:00","id":724804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724755#post724755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You were supposed to sympathize with First Edition Silver Pact <i>and </i>take it seriously. (That didn't work, but it was the intent.)<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact of Third Edition is very different. You CAN take them seriously, but you're not supposed to sympathize with what they're doing. Just like the Scarlet Dynasty, or the Sidereal Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>No kidding. Of course considering that the vast majority of people already knew that Lunars in 1e were in a fucked spot because of the 11th hour changes to them, to their disservice as well as as the unfortunate hardcover having Grabowski double down on the not only unflattering aspects of 1e Lunars but also the writing was just bad, offensive(and I don't use that word lightly), and not in tune with the sort of mythic and real world historical cues that the game tries to springboard off of. That you're not supposed to necessarily sympathize with a good chunk of the setting of Exalted in general without at least an &quot;It's a complicated situation.&quot; if you're familiar with the source material is, to me, rather obvious. To go back to Game of Thrones. Jaime Lannister is a character I and some friends have learned to enjoy later in the series but that doesn't mean we suddenly forgot all the awful things he did in his backstory of his earlier book screentime. I personally enjoy morally grey complexity....and this last bit is important for Exalted. WHEN IT'S DONE WELL. In that regard, 1e was anything but and comparison of 3e Lunars to it seem just a teeny tiny bit like hyperbole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-24-2015, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T20:03:29-07:00","id":724879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724155#post724155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iconoclasts do not need to be rebels - just to be in disagreement with how things <i>are</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think a rebel is?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I totally agree with you here. To my eyes, the Lunars appear to be about the journey <i>even more</i> than the destination in a way Solars, for instance, aren't. </div> </div> </div>...Uh, that's not what I get out of that.<br /> <br /> See, the Lunar Exalted CAN fix the situation, if they can manage to destroy the Scarlet Dynasty and do something about the Sidereal Exalted. If the Lunar Exalted can change the world so that they're not being hunted like animals by Usurpers and Despoilers of the First Age, then they lose at least half the source of their angst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T00:08:06-07:00","id":725293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724058#post724058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple things.<br /> <br /> 1. I don't think that's described as something ALL Lunars do, or that all Lunars go about it in the extreme realpolitik way I described. Certainly some do, but other Lunars probably go about their goals in other ways. The Silver Pact is not the monolith of the Bureau of Destiny, and making it less like the Garou Nation is great for all the reasons that making it the Garou Nation to begin with didn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've missed my point in the Sid comparison. I don't give a good goddamn how organized the Lunars are. I like organization, personally, but I don't think it's critical to a play experience.<br /> <br /> What <i>is</i> important is accomplishing something. We've had it mentioned that Sidereals will have Things To Do - holes in reality to patch, threats to avert, all manner of work that isn't connected to the Bronze-Gold Divide or other splats in general. We might not have any details, but even that much has me stoked - interesting hooks to take part in as a Sid, yay!<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Lunars at this point have a lot of RIP AND TEAR HUGE GUTS and one paragraph of lip service to 'Oh, yeah, you can totally do your own thing, too.' That... does not stoke me. That the <i>exact opposite</i> of stokes me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724058#post724058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. In a way I like the solid greying of morality in the Realm vs Lunar war thing. Lunars are not just some ancient good guys who the current government won't leave alone; they're doing terrible things to support their goals, <i>which is a strategy that human beings employ and always have employed.</i><br /> <br /> Why was their 2e &quot;morality,&quot; which to me seemed to be &quot;farcically ignore the actual state of Creation to stick our heads in the sand re mortal societies that will not be able to last without us,&quot; a better state?</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so, this I can explain.<br /> <br /> Step one - forget the actual <i>details</i> of the River. Which societies, the desired conditions, all of that. It wasn't well done, it's not the point.<br /> <br /> The point is <i>why the River existed</i>. It was the Lunars and their Elders looking at what had happened in the world, looking at the First Age and the current one and going, &quot;Y'know, none of this has worked properly. We need to find something better.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Nobody else in the setting did that</i>.<br /> <br /> It was always, 'Put Myself/Someone In Absolute Charge By Supreme Mandate And Don't Mess It Up This Time'. The New Realm and the Old were organized on the same fundamental principle of autocracy and top-down granting of boons. It's doing the same thing over and over and trying to get it right by sheer repetition without considering that <i>maybe that thing was the problem</i>.<br /> <br /> The River was asking, &quot;OK, what can work instead?&quot; and <i>trying</i> it. It's acknowledging that actually <i>fixing</i> the <i>causes</i> of 'the actual state of Creation' is an unavoidable necessity if you want to do more than just treat symptoms.<br /> <br /> And that is a <i>hell</i> of a play hook.<br /> <br /> Which is gone. And replaced by cynical terrorism, murder, and bloodlust.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=724058#post724058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, is this the true ideal version of the Lunar narrative. I dunno. Probably not? I'm really not sure, because we never have had a good alternative to compare it to. We can't look at it like Yozis and say &quot;I prefer the GoD portrayal to the MOEP Infernals and CoCD Malfeas one,&quot; because 1e Lunars was an example of total bedshitting and 2e Lunars was narratively incoherent. I'm not sure TAW even answered the narrative question, so much as its goal was to make the mechanics not &quot;Solar Charms, but overcosted and silver-colored.&quot;<br /> <br /> Are they now filling a niche that was unfilled, and better than the sloppy lack of direction, set on the boring edges of the world, that they had as a splat in the past? I say absolutely.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a niche I want no part of, and I'm deeply dismayed to see it happening to a splat I had previously quite liked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T00:28:54-07:00","id":725325,"title":"","content":"It would be cool if Solars were able to shape a society to their vision while Lunars were able to help a society flourish, but not control it.<br /> <br /> I expect many players would judge that as Lunars being weaker than Solars though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T00:39:56-07:00","id":725335,"title":"","content":"To build on Valles's point of &quot;It's not encouraging if that's ALL we see of them&quot;... Well, I imagine it's a bit like Archery charms.<br /> <br /> I think we can all agree that a lot of the Archery charms seem to be assuming you'll be using a bow. Like, a lot of them can apply to a crossbow, and many of them to a flame weapon, but it's <i>pretty</i> obvious that they're made with the mind of someone sniping with arrows shot from a bow. Like, how does the &quot;Set your arrow on FIRE!&quot; charm, the &quot;Make an arrow out of Essence&quot; charm, or the &quot;Shoot an arrow that sticks to something and only the Solar can remove it&quot; charm apply to a flame weapon?<br /> <br /> It can be tough to look at other interpretations when they're not presenting options FOR you. The Lunar writeup is presenting them in one major way, and it's not even giving a parallel to Righteous Devil Style, where we can go &quot;But if you want to use this non-standard Archery weapon, you can use this!&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, it's like if there WERE no Righteous Devil Style, and all we got was a box off to the side saying &quot;Some of these charms don't really mix well with using a Firewand. Well you totally can, just be creative!&quot;<br /> <br /> How something is presented can form a huge impact on how they're perceived, and most of the Lunar writeup paints them as falling into a major group of &quot;Consumed by rage&quot;. I fully believe that we'll get a much better writeup through the eyes of the Lunars in their book, but we don't <i>have</i> that book now. And for people unfamiliar with Lunars, what we have seems to put them into one camp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 10-25-2015, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T01:18:14-07:00","id":725386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=725325#post725325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be cool if Solars were able to shape a society to their vision while Lunars were able to help a society flourish, but not control it.<br /> <br /> I expect many players would judge that as Lunars being weaker than Solars though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, sounds to me like the Lunar society would be better! The Solar's got some kind of mad utopia going on, Communism or Fascism or whatever, and you're living in a society which is like it was before, only better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T02:21:39-07:00","id":725418,"title":"","content":"Well, I can see where that comes from because one of the images that the new edition is really clear on (and I think the language ties to Solars more clearly and logically to the concept than any edition before) is that players will choose to play a Solar &quot;<i>to be a forger of nations, armies, religions, wonders, or even worlds</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, yeah, I do feel like, how often do new nations and religions really need to be founded so much as working with what is there and making the old ones better? Won't new nations just arise naturally if there is a breakdown in the existing ones, and do even really need new nations and religions (societies) if not?<br /> <br /> But it's definitely a clear theme and part of what Solars are about. Maybe Creation is a place where working with the religions and nations that exist can only take you so far. Could you make the er... slave sorcerocracy of Ys a much better society without having founding a &quot;new&quot; nation? A better religion than the Immaculate Philosophy without founding a &quot;new&quot; religion? (Side note: The 3e Creation feels very rich in oppressive, predatory and hierarchical societies, in a way that is very classic / old school S&amp;S, and feels it probably has more emphasis on this than prior editions.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T04:24:40-07:00","id":725558,"title":"","content":"Had a friend who was kind enough to let me get a look at the backer PDF, so now things are easier.<br /> <br /> My reading of the Lunar text is the Old Ways are dead. The Bond shattered, and while that freed the Lunars to an extent, it also hurt them. The Bond was replaced with Rage. The text literally talks about them being driven to tear down the things and people that stole what was once theirs. The &quot;never going back&quot; thing sounds more like Lunars as a group are not interested in restoring the Solar Deliberative., rather than the death of the Bond itself.<br /> <br /> So, I'm thinking the Bond is still a thing(especially given that all the dev statements indicates it's staying), but some Lunars either have no Bond, or the Bond is replaced by another mechanic focused around this vengeance/rage angle. It makes sense, really. When the incredibly powerful magical bond that connected you to someone is destroyed, there is a metaphysical hole in your being. Where you once were compelled to love, protect, and guide, now you feel compelled to lash out at those who severed your Bond.<br /> <br /> I can see shades of the same ideas in the other splat examples. The Liminals are drawn to the unquiet dead and told to destroy them. The Abyssals follow the chivalry of death. These both feel like setting explanations for Limit mechanics.<br /> <br /> So, in a few years, we will have a Lunar book, and there will be a Bond, and I will laugh merrily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T04:32:10-07:00","id":725563,"title":"","content":"The Bond is present in a Solar integrity charm, funnily enough it's a charm that says &quot;This defense is inapplicable against your Lunar mate, due to your bond.&quot; or something to that effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T06:22:15-07:00","id":725764,"title":"","content":"The concept of the Bond going both ways such as to allow the Lunars to temper the judgement and actions of the Solars in much the same as Luna tempers the Unconquered Sun's light and gives Creation repose from it has a lot of potential, in my opinion. It makes Lunars more than the right hands and devoted sidekicks of the Solars where the Bond is applicable. It makes them partners who can question and better their mate, Enkidu to Gilgamesh.<br /> <br /> And it might play rather nicely to Luna's standards and ideals for her Chosen. Lunars were made in the chains of bondage, but she only chooses those with the ability to free themselves. They were made to be the seconds of the Solars, but they can be more. They have the power to become something in Creation that is not defined by the Solars. They already are, which is why many look on the return of the Solars with anxiety. They've changed. For the better or for worse none can say yet, but the fact is they changed <i>without the Solars</i>, and they don't want to be forced to turn back now.<br /> <br /> On a different topic, I thought the Thousand Streams River was an interesting Lunar <i>ideal</i>, even if its execution left something to be desired. I wouldn't mind seeing it return in some form, especially if it adds to Lunars without cheapening anything else in the setting. The Silver Pact isn't a homogenous entity with a singular mind, even if they irrevocably share the objective of bringing down the Realm by definition; so you'd think that some will ponder what to do next after they have achieved their goal, a train of thought from which I can see the Thousand Streams River developing and becoming a factor in the minds of the elders that not all agree with.<br /> <br /> And we really shouldn't already judge everything about Lunars so early when their write-up in the core likely doesn't have everything they're about. The Sidereal write up certainly doesn't specify any of the threats to Fate that they deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 10-25-2015, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T08:17:31-07:00","id":726028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=725764#post725764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The concept of the Bond going both ways such as to allow the Lunars to temper the judgement and actions of the Solars in much the same as Luna tempers the Unconquered Sun's light and gives Creation repose from it has a lot of potential, in my opinion. It makes Lunars more than the right hands and devoted sidekicks of the Solars where the Bond is applicable. It makes them partners who can question and better their mate, Enkidu to Gilgamesh.<br /> <br /> And it might play rather nicely to Luna's standards and ideals for her Chosen. Lunars were made in the chains of bondage, but she only chooses those with the ability to free themselves. They were made to be the seconds of the Solars, but they can be more. They have the power to become something in Creation that is not defined by the Solars. They already are, which is why many look on the return of the Solars with anxiety. They've changed. For the better or for worse none can say yet, but the fact is they changed <i>without the Solars</i>, and they don't want to be forced to turn back now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have anything to say to this except that I agree, and so strongly that I feel like removing it from my quote would be a disservice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=725764#post725764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different topic, I thought the Thousand Streams River was an interesting Lunar <i>ideal</i>, even if its execution left something to be desired. I wouldn't mind seeing it return in some form, especially if it adds to Lunars without cheapening anything else in the setting. The Silver Pact isn't a homogenous entity with a singular mind, even if they irrevocably share the objective of bringing down the Realm by definition; so you'd think that some will ponder what to do next after they have achieved their goal, a train of thought from which I can see the Thousand Streams River developing and becoming a factor in the minds of the elders that not all agree with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the Silver Pact is generally about hurting the Realm: this doesn't mean, as others have pointed out, that that is <i>all</i> that a Silver Pact Lunar <i>does</i>. I imagine that some of them might do simpler/different things in off time - maybe they raise families of beast men, or court spirits (literally), or do things that try to make the world a better place. None of this is in disagreement with the Silver Pact's goals, but I think it's really important to note that all of the Lunars are individuals first and foremost - I imagine that the Pact is just a way to ensure that they can more easily aid one another in their mostly mutual goals of tearing down the Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=725764#post725764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we really shouldn't already judge everything about Lunars so early when their write-up in the core likely doesn't have everything they're about. The Sidereal write up certainly doesn't specify any of the threats to Fate that they deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Very much this. Before we go into panic spirals via Internet echo chamber, recall that what we <i>know</i> is extremely limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":7858,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","user":"*End","date":". 10-25-2015, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:00:33-07:00","id":726177,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that the flipside of Rage is Despair.<br /> <br /> Consider Kratos, of <i>God of War</i>. A man so depressed from accidentally murdering his wife and child that he throws himself into more murderous anger to have a reason to live. And when he has no one left to murder, his despair returns in full force and he tries to commit suicide.<br /> <br /> Consider the Garou, of <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i>. Gifted with the curse of Luna's supernatural Rage in order to fight an endless battle against the Wyrm to save Gaia, a werewolf who loses hope falls into Hirano, a deep despair that immunizes them against Rage but leaves them without the motivation to do anything, and puts them on Suicide Watch.<br /> <br /> <br /> But just as we don't expect Raging Lunars to be universally furious to the point of insanity, neither does Despair mean a sad Lunar need to be suicidal.<br /> <br /> Consider Sadness, of Pixar's <i>Inside Out</i>. Her job was never simply to make her person feel sad, miserable, and hopeless. Her job was about sympathy. When someone is feeling sad, others can see the signs of her misery even when the person doesn't know how to communicate them, and they will come to help. But also, your memories of sadness give you the ability to understand the pain of others. Further, if you couldn't become sad about another person's sadness, what would motivate you to make them happy?<br /> <br /> <br /> The Lunars who focus their attention on the Realm, they're angry. They aim to kill, destroy, and take back what is theirs.<br /> <br /> The Lunars who don't focus on the Realm could very well be sad. They aim to save, to build, and to create a new place removed from all of the fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:07:15-07:00","id":726187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=725293#post725293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is <i>why the River existed</i>. It was the Lunars and their Elders looking at what had happened in the world, looking at the First Age and the current one and going, &quot;Y'know, none of this has worked properly. We need to find something better.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Nobody else in the setting did that</i>.<br /> <br /> It was always, 'Put Myself/Someone In Absolute Charge By Supreme Mandate And Don't Mess It Up This Time'. The New Realm and the Old were organized on the same fundamental principle of autocracy and top-down granting of boons. It's doing the same thing over and over and trying to get it right by sheer repetition without considering that <i>maybe that thing was the problem</i>.<br /> <br /> The River was asking, &quot;OK, what can work instead?&quot; and <i>trying</i> it. It's acknowledging that actually <i>fixing</i> the <i>causes</i> of 'the actual state of Creation' is an unavoidable necessity if you want to do more than just treat symptoms.<br /> <br /> And that is a <i>hell</i> of a play hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>While a great plot hook, it still made no sense in the actual context of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=725293#post725293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a niche I want no part of, and I'm deeply dismayed to see it happening to a splat I had previously quite liked.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did you like about them exactly? Anything aside from what was in the your last post?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:10:42-07:00","id":726212,"title":"","content":"Thinking of Lunars as raging iconoclasts kinda makes me wants to see a band of Lunars punks rocking the oppressive realm into suubmission. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still, what bugs me is that with so much focus on destroying the main power keeping the forces of Darkness out of Creation, with not a hint of an intent to put something in its place, the Silver Pact looks like they've not really thought things through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:48:09-07:00","id":726323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=726028#post726028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of this is in disagreement with the Silver Pact's goals, but I think it's really important to note that all of the Lunars are individuals first and foremost - I imagine that the Pact is just a way to ensure that they can more easily aid one another in their mostly mutual goals of tearing down the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. I think it even mentions that &quot;huge organisations&quot; isn't something that really comes to them naturally - Luna's gifts are great if you want to fight as a loose assortment of unpredictable guerrilla, but it's not exactly helpful in creating a huge hierachical structure.<br /> <br /> So the Silver Pact is just the &quot;label&quot; for Lunars tearing down the Realm, each their own way, with the only &quot;conformity&quot; coming from the fact that, well, their abilities come from the same source, some approaches have been shown to be rather effective, and, well, the old Lunars are happy to teach the younger ones how to do things the way they do.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, yeah, they don't seem to have plans yet for what to do once the Realm crumbles. But then, there are countless countries all around the threshold doing fine - and who would probably do even better if the Realm didn't try to keep them small and harmless - so they don't really <i>have</i> to. The Immaculate Order sells the Realm as the one defence against everything. The Lunars simply disagree, and I think there's enough wiggle room in the setting to leave it open whether they're right or wrong.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T10:43:24-07:00","id":726480,"title":"","content":"Harano isn't actually immunity from Rage, it is a manifestation of it. Rage produces more extreme emotional reactions than humans can fathom, and Harano is when it swings toward unremitting sadness, which mechanically halves all of your dice pools unless you spend one wp per scene. Losing the Wolf/$ANIMAL is when you're cut off from/immune to Rage, but only until you regain a Willpower point naturally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=726212#post726212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking of Lunars as raging iconoclasts kinda makes me wants to see a band of Lunars punks rocking the oppressive realm into suubmission. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still, what bugs me is that with so much focus on destroying the main power keeping the forces of Darkness out of Creation, with not a hint of an intent to put something in its place, the Silver Pact looks like they've not really thought things through.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm isn't keeping anything out of Creation. The Empress killed the Fair Folk en masse, once, and caused a lot of collateral damage in the process. The Fair Folk aren't going to rise up again like that, and the Deathlords aren't out to commit Double Omnicide. The only Deathlord that's out to cause trouble is the Mask, and the River Province is the one typically trying to keep a check on him. You know, that place that the Realm tried to invade repeatedly and for which it still has some designs of conquest? They're the ones cleaning that mess up. The Realm is just tax-farming and turning inward. The transition toward disorder has already begun, and the Blessed Isle is not going to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:07:45-07:00","id":726538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=726187#post726187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a great plot hook, it still made no sense in the actual context of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are mistaken, sir. The basic pattern recognition to link together the fact that every previously failed attempt at organizing society and Creation shared certain traits is hardly nonsensical, especially coming from the Exalted. Deciding that they don't want to spend their multimillenial lifespans engaged in an act of insanity ('Trying the same thing over again and expecting a different result'), or to live through yet another major societal crash, requires only self-interest.<br /> <br /> Now, you can certainly say that, while not an act of Randian Perfect Rationality, continuing to feud with the Sidereals and the Realm over something that long-ago became irrelevant is very plausible, very <i>human</i>, and I won't disagree. I am saying that the increase in setting coherence comes at the expense of play interest, and that that means that calling existing 3e direction an untrammeled improvement, rather than at best mixed, is simply false.<br /> <br /> Lunars did need a lot of refinement. But 'refinement' and 'improvement' are not necessarily synonyms, and, though I agree with *End and YeOfLittleFaith that it's far, far too soon to speak conclusively, and I have enough support for my faith in the developers' judgement to feel a reasonable expectation that they <i>have</i> considered 'positive' plot hooks and will be including them in future Lunar-focused material...<br /> <br /> The <i>current</i> state of the tea leaves does not look promising.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=726187#post726187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did you like about them exactly? Anything aside from what was in the your last post?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having someone in the setting actually at least <i>trying</i> to think ahead was pretty much it. I enjoyed shapeshifting as a concept and a tactical hook, but that doesn't seem to be going anywhere as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:38:05-07:00","id":726587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=726538#post726538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic pattern recognition to link together the fact that every previously failed attempt at organizing society and Creation shared certain traits is hardly nonsensical, especially coming from the Exalted. Deciding that they don't want to spend their multimillenial lifespans engaged in an act of insanity ('Trying the same thing over again and expecting a different result'), or to live through yet another major societal crash, requires only self-interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, it every (Exalted-ruled) society in creation had somehow crumbled on its own, that would be true. But so far, the reasons the various cultures crumbled weren't some obscure, inevitable forces of nature, but easy to make out problems.<br /> <br /> The Primordial rule got crushed because the Exalted wanted them to stop ruling.<br /> The Solar rule got crushed because other Exalts wanted them to stop ruling.<br /> The Shogunate rule ended because of two simultaneous end-of-the-world events.<br /> The Realm - yeah, in 2ed, it kinda fell into decline on its own. In 3ed, it's in decline because Exalts want them to stop ruling.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I can see how &quot;Exalts&quot; are a common factor (three out of four), but not in the sense of &quot;It's bad to put them in charge&quot; - all but the Shogunate were perfectly stable until Exalted wanted to end them. (And the fall of the Shogunate was caused by something none of the Thousand Stream River projects could possibly protect itself against, either.)<br /> The common thing is that when any kind of Exalts come together to topple the current social order, they have a scary effective track record. The Thousand Streams River? It just gives Exalts <i>softer targets</i>. That doesn't exactly seem like planing ahead. And removing Exalts completely? It leaves the World entirely unprepared for the next Contagion/Balorian Crusade.<br /> <br /> <br /> One &quot;reasonable&quot; approach would be to lock up all dissenting Exalts, but look how that worked out in the case of Solars.<br /> <br /> Another approach would be to find a way to make sure all Exalts somehow work together, and make sure no group feels its only option is the complete overthrow of society as a whole, because, well, they might just succeed. But the Lunars still have a grudge and don't seem to be all that interested in reconciliation, so maybe they're not the right ones to sell that angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:43:05-07:00","id":726625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=726587#post726587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another approach would be to find a way to make sure all Exalts somehow work together, and make sure no group feels its only option is the complete overthrow of society as a whole, because, well, they might just succeed. But the Lunars still have a grudge and don't seem to be all that interested in reconciliation, so maybe they're not the right ones to sell that angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, I do have an idea about a Lunar concept I kind of want to play - one with a Sidereal lover/friend who wants to reconcile the two sorts of Celestials to focus on other things (like maybe stopping the spiraling negativity that Creation is going through).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:00:47-07:00","id":726681,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Lunars and the idea of people in the world trying to do things to move it forward (heart this), I was a little disappointed by the Caul as described. Don't get me wrong, it still gets me tons rev'd up, but with the talk of how the Lunars disconnected the continent from the structure of Fate, I was hoping to hear more about what they *do* there to build a better world, rather than so much of the bloody wars for cities, which the Lunars control in order to drain the world of its Dragonbloodlines. Perhaps this will come in the Lunars book, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:01:31-07:00","id":726685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=726480#post726480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harano isn't actually immunity from Rage, it is a manifestation of it. Rage produces more extreme emotional reactions than humans can fathom, and Harano is when it swings toward unremitting sadness, which mechanically halves all of your dice pools unless you spend one wp per scene. Losing the Wolf/$ANIMAL is when you're cut off from/immune to Rage, but only until you regain a Willpower point naturally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Realm isn't keeping anything out of Creation. The Empress killed the Fair Folk en masse, once, and caused a lot of collateral damage in the process. The Fair Folk aren't going to rise up again like that, and the Deathlords aren't out to commit Double Omnicide. The only Deathlord that's out to cause trouble is the Mask, and the River Province is the one typically trying to keep a check on him. You know, that place that the Realm tried to invade repeatedly and for which it still has some designs of conquest? They're the ones cleaning that mess up. The Realm is just tax-farming and turning inward. The transition toward disorder has already begun, and the Blessed Isle is not going to help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because the setting isn't focused on preventing imminent Armageddon anymore doesn't mean the Fae, the Dead, the Demons and who know what aren't intent on turning Creation into their personal playground. The scale is merely reduced.<br /> The Realm and its Dragon-Blooded still help keep some sort of order on Creation, regulating the activity of gods and elementals, keeping ancestor cults in line, slaying rampaging gods and rakshas. Lunars and their barbarians canon fodder can't really do this as efficiently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:27:07-07:00","id":726727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=726685#post726685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just because the setting isn't focused on preventing imminent Armageddon anymore doesn't mean the Fae, the Dead, the Demons and who know what aren't intent on turning Creation into their personal playground. The scale is merely reduced.<br /> The Realm and its Dragon-Blooded still help keep some sort of order on Creation, regulating the activity of gods and elementals, keeping ancestor cults in line, slaying rampaging gods and rakshas. Lunars and their barbarians canon fodder can't really do this as efficiently.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a past tense. At this point, the Realm is demanding money but not really providing much in the way of order or stabilization. Everyone's in a foot race to get to the throne first, and the Threshold is getting left in the cold. Anyone who's putting their faith in the Dynasty to solve problems is going to be sorely disappointed. And if they do come back, it's going to be even more of the same, because anyone that sits on the throne of a lessened Scarlet Empire is going to be a few degrees removed from the vantage point of the Empress, and is likely going to double down on the same institutional failings. Terrible fates abound; best to get the ball rolling on defeating the empire before they recover to come back and put you in chains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:29:36-07:00","id":726729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=726685#post726685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm and its Dragon-Blooded still help keep some sort of order on Creation, regulating the activity of gods and elementals, keeping ancestor cults in line, slaying rampaging gods and rakshas. Lunars and their barbarians canon fodder can't really do this as efficiently.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, there are vast places in the world the Realm can't reach, yet which stay reasonably safe non the less.<br /> <br /> Which is why I think there's room for both interpretations - that the Realm really is the best/only way to keep Creation safe, a haven of stability keeping the world safe... or that it's just that one center of power in the middle of the world, which is superfluous to the stability of the borders since those had to get by on their own for centuries, anyway.<br /> Which one is true is probably better left to the table instead of being nailed down in canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:47:24-07:00","id":726765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=726727#post726727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a past tense. At this point, the Realm is demanding money but not really providing much in the way of order or stabilization. Everyone's in a foot race to get to the throne first, and the Threshold is getting left in the cold. Anyone who's putting their faith in the Dynasty to solve problems is going to be sorely disappointed. And if they do come back, it's going to be even more of the same, because anyone that sits on the throne of a lessened Scarlet Empire is going to be a few degrees removed from the vantage point of the Empress, and is likely going to double down on the same institutional failings. Terrible fates abound; best to get the ball rolling on defeating the empire before they recover to come back and put you in chains.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a recent issue, though. The Silver Pact was doing its thing for a long time before the Empress disappeared.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T17:00:44-07:00","id":733428,"title":"","content":"I've always liked the idea of Lunars, but they've always had a few fundamental problems. Like if you proportionally reduced their essence pools and charm essence costs they'd be on par with Terrestrials. In fact ultimately, Lunars were a kind of terrestrial exalt with animal aspects. Basically using your totem as an aspect. They were the chosen of animals. The new 3rd edition core book suggests very little real change in this. So, I'm wondering;<br /> <br /> What thematic concept makes Lunars a <b><i><u>Celestial</u></i></b> Exalted.<br /> <br /> What miracle makes them on par with Solars or Sidereals .<br /> Solars are epically perfect and change the world around them with their power.<br /> Sidereals are the lords of fate and the world changes to their designs<br /> Lunars shapeshift into a living bulldozer and change the world slowly and physically???<br /> Dragon-blooded wield the elements changing the world by force.<br /> <br /> Lunars have never had a theme like this to show their impact on the world. Even the stories in the core seem to leave Lunars as an afterthought among the exalteds' effect on the world. I'm not looking for specifics, yet, but I'd like to know what the Lunars' miraculous theme is going to be. Right now I'm just going to prepare myself for my exalted type to continue to remain as terrestrial-level power.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T17:40:25-07:00","id":733513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=733428#post733428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always liked the idea of Lunars, but they've always had a few fundamental problems. Like if you proportionally reduced their essence pools and charm essence costs they'd be on par with Terrestrials. In fact ultimately, Lunars were a kind of terrestrial exalt with animal aspects. Basically using your totem as an aspect. They were the chosen of animals. The new 3rd edition core book suggests very little real change in this. So, I'm wondering;<br /> <br /> What thematic concept makes Lunars a <b><i><u>Celestial</u></i></b> Exalted.<br /> <br /> What miracle makes them on par with Solars or Sidereals .<br /> Solars are epically perfect and change the world around them with their power.<br /> Sidereals are the lords of fate and the world changes to their designs<br /> Lunars shapeshift into a living bulldozer and change the world slowly and physically???<br /> Dragon-blooded wield the elements changing the world by force.<br /> <br /> Lunars have never had a theme like this to show their impact on the world. Even the stories in the core seem to leave Lunars as an afterthought among the exalteds' effect on the world. I'm not looking for specifics, yet, but I'd like to know what the Lunars' miraculous theme is going to be. Right now I'm just going to prepare myself for my exalted type to continue to remain as terrestrial-level power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars are the reason that Creation is a swords and sorcery affair with monstrous Anathema lurking in the wilderness instead of a Jack Kirby wonderland that conspicuously lacks Lunars. The only reason that Terrestrials can manage to fight them, and have kept them away, is because the Terrestrials are leaning on relics of the Jack Kirby wonderland, and more of those objects of power are lost or ruined with each passing year. Eventually, the combined orchestration of Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded will fall before the Lunars, because the Lunars don't need the legacy of the Solars to defeat their foes, if their foes don't have it any more, either.<br /> <br /> That's been the stated direction for years, now. The link to most of the material describing it is near the start of the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T17:48:19-07:00","id":733518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=733513#post733513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars are the reason that Creation is a swords and sorcery affair with monstrous Anathema lurking in the wilderness instead of a Jack Kirby wonderland that conspicuously lacks Lunars. The only reason that Terrestrials can manage to fight them, and have kept them away, is because the Terrestrials are leaning on relics of the Jack Kirby wonderland, and more of those objects of power are lost or ruined with each passing year. Eventually, the combined orchestration of Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded will fall before the Lunars, because the Lunars don't need the legacy of the Solars to defeat their foes, if their foes don't have it any more, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Furthermore, I think that the Lunars are the Chosen who have been hit hardest by the events since their inception, while remaining around to deal with the consequences. They've been beaten, kicked off their pedestals, lost their leaders, friends, lovers, and spouses, lost the world where they knew what they were, and <i>still</i> they continued, changing to better suit their new time. The Lunars are hunted by a collusion of Sidereal and Dragon-Blooded forces whenever a new one is Chosen, but have managed to create and maintain their domains across Creation despite that. They are, insofar as any splat is, unbent, unbroken by the sheer amount of crap they've cone through as a group. Once they were the mates of the rulers of Creation, their second-in-commands, their guardians and their most trusted allies. They are not any longer, and with that place lost, they seek to carve out a new one in a world that hates them and moreover, <i>fears</i> them. The Lunars endure, and keep pushing back against it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":7858,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","user":"*End","date":".  Clarifying sentence structure. 10-27-2015, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T19:06:35-07:00","id":733693,"title":"","content":"I've read those links before. You're pointing out what they've done/endured and that's interesting, but what is the overall theme that made them majestic? How did they stand next to the other Celestial Exalted? Or even, if you took the Lunars out of the story, what of the historical plot would change? In the new core book they are little more than a speed bump to the Fair Folk invasion. Just saying that they are monsters doesn't give them the Celestial majesty similar to the other Celestials. Saying that they've been trampled by the world doesn't make them demigods. What I'm asking is what makes them shine like their Celestial brethren or are they more like Terrestrials? Not shining but still majestic. So far they still sound more like Terrestrials than Celestials and their minimal effect on the historical plot is not helping to counteract this view.<br /> The overall theme I want to know is not the theme of the Lunars in general. Just the theme that makes them NOT Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Did this make ANY sense? I'm not sure it did.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T19:38:57-07:00","id":733718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=733693#post733693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the new core book they are little more than a speed bump to the Fair Folk invasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's absolutely not what the new Lunars are. I don't think the idea of Lunars vs Fair Folk is even mentioned once. They're the terrible beasts that tear at the edges of civilisation, who are used by parents to frighten their children into going to bed on time and feared by the Realm's legions even when they were in the prime. Now they're the warlords of barbarian hordes who threaten to overrun all the Threshold in a great tide of fur and claw while the Dynasts play their meaningless political games. I don't know where you could get this idea of Lunars being a speed bump to the Fair Folk unless you accidentally opened up the 2e corebook instead of the 3e one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T21:21:37-07:00","id":733877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=733693#post733693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read those links before. You're pointing out what they've done/endured and that's interesting, but what is the overall theme that made them majestic? How did they stand next to the other Celestial Exalted? Or even, if you took the Lunars out of the story, what of the historical plot would change? In the new core book they are little more than a speed bump to the Fair Folk invasion. Just saying that they are monsters doesn't give them the Celestial majesty similar to the other Celestials. Saying that they've been trampled by the world doesn't make them demigods. What I'm asking is what makes them shine like their Celestial brethren or are they more like Terrestrials? Not shining but still majestic. So far they still sound more like Terrestrials than Celestials and their minimal effect on the historical plot is not helping to counteract this view.<br /> The overall theme I want to know is not the theme of the Lunars in general. Just the theme that makes them NOT Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Did this make ANY sense? I'm not sure it did.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to be a matter of taste in aesthetics. Lunars are decidedly more physically concrete and less abstract in approach to power and theme than Solars or Siderals, but so are Alchemicals. You can think of Lunars as being to beasts as Alchemicals are to machines, in some capacity. You might not think that a giant eel from the west is very impressive, but a Lunar will use this shape to shock the hell out of you nonetheless, not unlike how a Solar looking merely human isn't quite so impressive at first glance, or how the mere human appearance provides no hint that the Solar can kick you through several carriages. After all, would that not also fling the Solar back even farther?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T06:45:53-07:00","id":734562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=733718#post733718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's absolutely not what the new Lunars are. I don't think the idea of Lunars vs Fair Folk is even mentioned once. They're the terrible beasts that tear at the edges of civilisation, who are used by parents to frighten their children into going to bed on time and feared by the Realm's legions even when they were in the prime. Now they're the warlords of barbarian hordes who threaten to overrun all the Threshold in a great tide of fur and claw while the Dynasts play their meaningless political games. I don't know where you could get this idea of Lunars being a speed bump to the Fair Folk unless you accidentally opened up the 2e corebook instead of the 3e one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ex3 Core Book Pg. 22 paragraph 2<br /> &quot;Even the mighty Lunar Exalted, the former mates of the Solars, could do little more than slow their monstrous advance.&quot;<br /> <br /> Saur Ops,<br /> to be honest, I kinda see Alchemicals the same way. More as a high end Terrestrial, and since they're considered a low end Celestial in game it's not much of a stretch. The fact that they're more numerous and are formed from a Primordial's essence like the Terrestrials adds to this. However, I kinda see your point there it just seems to me that Celestials should have <i>Miracles.</i> The Solars have Solar circle sorcery, the Sidereals have Sidereal Martial Arts and Astrology and even the Alchemicals have God-Machine Protocols(yes, I know I just contradicted myself). These things produce <i>Miracles</i> in the world. Lunars don't really have this. Their shapeshifting is impressive but it is still only about on par with the elemental forces of the Terrestrials. What is their <i>Miracle?</i><br /> <br /> And now I feel like a Vorlon from Babylon 5 asking the Lunars over and over again; &quot;Who are you?&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway, I doubt I'm going to get a satisfactory answer, certainly not until the Lunar book comes out in, what, ten years? Until then I'll just enjoy my terrestrial Chosen of Animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:18:04-07:00","id":734648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=734562#post734562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ex3 Core Book Pg. 22 paragraph 2<br /> &quot;Even the mighty Lunar Exalted, the former mates of the Solars, could do little more than slow their monstrous advance.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The metatextual setup for the Balorian Crusade is &quot;another apocalypse happens on the heels of the first one&quot;. No one was meant to be able to halt it in the setup; nine out of every ten living things had just died, and the numbers of the Exalted were also kind of thinned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> to be honest, I kinda see Alchemicals the same way. More as a high end Terrestrial, and since they're considered a low end Celestial in game it's not much of a stretch. The fact that they're more numerous and are formed from a Primordial's essence like the Terrestrials adds to this. However, I kinda see your point there it just seems to me that Celestials should have <i>Miracles.</i> The Solars have Solar circle sorcery, the Sidereals have Sidereal Martial Arts and Astrology and even the Alchemicals have God-Machine Protocols(yes, I know I just contradicted myself). These things produce <i>Miracles</i> in the world. Lunars don't really have this. Their shapeshifting is impressive but it is still only about on par with the elemental forces of the Terrestrials. What is their <i>Miracle?</i><br /> <br /> And now I feel like a Vorlon from Babylon 5 asking the Lunars over and over again; &quot;Who are you?&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway, I doubt I'm going to get a satisfactory answer, certainly not until the Lunar book comes out in, what, ten years? Until then I'll just enjoy my terrestrial Chosen of Animals. </div> </div> </div>If you don't think that shapeshifting is impressive, then you don't think that shapeshifting is impressive, and I can't really give you an explanation that you're likely to accept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:36:35-07:00","id":734676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=734562#post734562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ex3 Core Book Pg. 22 paragraph 2<br /> &quot;Even the mighty Lunar Exalted, the former mates of the Solars, could do little more than slow their monstrous advance.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Balorian Crusade. <i>Everyone</i> was just a speed bump for the Fair Folk back then.<br /> <br /> That being said, the question &quot;What are Lunars? What should they be?&quot; has grown a beard <i>thiiiis</i> long, and I'm not sure if it's possible to say anything new there.<br /> Still, from what I've read, they're not just supposed to be &quot;animals&quot;. They take animal shapes, yes, but they're <i>mystical monsters</i>. And one thing that seems to set them appat from all other Exalts so far is - when the world changed, so did they. &quot;Change yourself to change the world&quot; and stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T08:16:15-07:00","id":734820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=734648#post734648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't think that shapeshifting is impressive, then you don't think that shapeshifting is impressive, and I can't really give you an explanation that you're likely to accept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what Smiles is saying is that &quot;I can reshape the world with my third circle sorcery&quot; of the Solars and the &quot;my day to day job is to keep the laws of nature and causality working and I know all loopholes to exploit them&quot; of the Sidereals is much more goal-oriented than the Lunars &quot;well, I can shapechange and ... uh ... was around in the last age too. Yay me?&quot;. The Lunars have a unique tool but the only thing they seem to use it for is totally reactive - destroy the Realm.<br /> <br /> Lunars are desperately in need of something they can actively do. All human societies, without any exception, and in fact all forms of life are hardwired to preserve and better themselves. Making Lunars to mere rage-fulled warriors makes them kind of unrealistic. They need to be able to build and enhance stuff, both literally and metaphorically - and just because they are animal-inspired doesn't change that. Over at rpg.net I once suggested a charm called &quot;Million Souls Home&quot; which allows them to instinctively build working homes and infrastructure for lots of people ... as do termites.<br /> Lunars should be able to create a highly effective but subconsciously working learning-by-imitation/play strategy for people, like a cat-mother bringing half-dead mice to her kittens. They should be able to whalesing helpful or manipulative memes into existence which pop up at the same time in multiple, far away places. They should be able to slowly, passively but irreversibely make their surrounding more supportive to life - not like a Solar plopping down a palace via sorcerous working, but like the roots of a tree slowly breaking and eroding stone to fertile earth.<br /> <br /> And besides something they can actively do, Lunars need something great they have actively DONE. Mate and companion to Solars is ok and fine - but at the moment they look more like trophy wives. There is no problem at all with being the minor half of a legendary pair, if it's done right: Enkidu was never as protagonist-y as Gilgamesh, but the story had enough points to make Enkidu a vital part of the story. Lunars are missing something like that when the game talks about the age when the celestial exalted still ruled Creation. The Solar ruled and created wonders, the Sidereals kept the world running and do so today. And the Lunars ... well ... most likely they helped to rule the world? Or built some smaller wonders? Maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T10:04:34-07:00","id":735107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=733428#post733428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always liked the idea of Lunars, but they've always had a few fundamental problems. Like if you proportionally reduced their essence pools and charm essence costs they'd be on par with Terrestrials. In fact ultimately, Lunars were a kind of terrestrial exalt with animal aspects. Basically using your totem as an aspect. They were the chosen of animals. The new 3rd edition core book suggests very little real change in this. So, I'm wondering;<br /> <br /> What thematic concept makes Lunars a <b><i><u>Celestial</u></i></b> Exalted.<br /> <br /> What miracle makes them on par with Solars or Sidereals .<br /> Solars are epically perfect and change the world around them with their power.<br /> Sidereals are the lords of fate and the world changes to their designs<br /> Lunars shapeshift into a living bulldozer and change the world slowly and physically???<br /> Dragon-blooded wield the elements changing the world by force.<br /> <br /> Lunars have never had a theme like this to show their impact on the world. Even the stories in the core seem to leave Lunars as an afterthought among the exalteds' effect on the world. I'm not looking for specifics, yet, but I'd like to know what the Lunars' miraculous theme is going to be. Right now I'm just going to prepare myself for my exalted type to continue to remain as terrestrial-level power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> Lunars as they've been implemented in1e and 2e never felt like they had any business being Celestial Exalts on par with Solars or Sidereals, Exalts who embodies fundamental concepts and manifest powers of cosmic significance, like Solar Circle Sorcery and Sidereal Martial Arts. The Lunars? not so much.<br /> Not only that, but they remain kind of useless, like they only exist to complete a set. You'd think Luna made them only because all the cool Incarnae were doing it.<br /> <br /> Also, one thing that annoyed me with Lunars was the lack of significance of their shapeshifting.<br /> It doesn't help them accomplish a given fuction, it has nothing to do with spiritual understanding or metaphysical ability. It's just a gimmick. A potentially useful and versatile one, but still a gimmick. This needs to change this time around. This power literally changes who and what they are everytime they use it, it should be more than a tool, it should have deep, real meaning. the Sacred Hunt was a tiny nod to this idea, I think but frankly who felt like this silly ritual was an important part of being a Lunar? It often felt more like a hindrance than anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T14:23:17-07:00","id":735814,"title":"","content":"So, my thoughts on the matter...not all of this is canon, a bunch of it is my thoughts on how it should be, and how I represent them.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lunar 'Miracle.'</b><br /> I think they are off to an okay start with Shapechanging (and the nature associated with it) being the 'core' of the Lunar Exalted, I just don't think they took it far enough. Beyond just changing form...a Lunar should be fully capable of 'becoming' something else. When they become an animal, it comes with the full kit of instincts and reflexes that the animal would have. But that's just the tip of the iceberg. As they grow in power, the extent to which they 'become' a form is a choice. At the most basic, they simply adopt the shape, but as they delve deeper into becoming that form, the more like it they are. Eventually, at the height of their power, they can truly become anything or anyone. For example, if a Lunar took the Heart's Blood of a guardsman and chose to fully 'become' that form, they would gain access to the former guardsman's memories, access to his intimacies (and the ability to temporarily adopt them as your own), and would fully adopt the guardsman's personality as their own. And, as their power grows beyond the need to take Heart's Blood, and can make due temporarily with just a sample, allowing them to temporarily become someone else, without having to kill that person. And a powerful enough Lunar is not even limited to mortal things.<br /> <br /> In Social terms, the same concept of 'change' would apply. A Lunar could rewire their mentality at will in order to become the best person possible to win this argument. This was often used to great effect in the First Age, where the Lunars could play the perfect Devil's Advocate for their mates by literally changing themselves into a person who believed what they needed to argue. Furthermore, if a Lunar was losing an argument, they could simply become someone to whom that argument would slide off of them. But that's only when a Lunar decides to argue with you to your face...<br /> <br /> On a grand scheme, regarding their powers beyond &quot;I can turn into other things,&quot; I think they should have abilities that primarily work on an instinctive (sub-conscious), animalistic, and group-based mechanic. While a Solar would look at a project that doesn't have enough skilled laborers to work on it, shrug, and do it all himself...a Lunar may grant a number of mortals an instinctive understanding of how to assist with the project. Solars are great at inspiring people to follow them, Lunars would instead bind people into a tight-knit pack that pursues a common goal, rather than a person. If a Solar wants to provide housing for a group of people, they'll slap it together overnight, or just conjure it up with Sorcery...a Lunar would influence the people to operate with the instinctive efficiency of an ant colony to construct their own housing.<br /> <br /> And, to build on the commentary made about Lunars and being Slaves...I do think that Lunars should have the widest variety of ways by which they can go 'you can't control me,' whether physical or social...<br /> <br /> <b>The Role of the Lunars</b><br /> I see the Lunars as the counterpoint to the Solars. Each are complete on their own, but the two compliment one another so well that they may wonder how they functioned before. A Solar is implacable, a Lunar is flexible. A Solar leads from the top, a Lunar builds up the people. A Solar is resolute and unchanging, a Lunar adapts on the fly. The actions of the Lunars may be eclipsed by those of the Solars, because what a Lunar doesn't isn't as in your face and obvious as what a Solar does. The Solars dreamed of an Empire and built it with their own hands...but the Lunars built the society into something that could support what the Solars had wrought. In fact, by this standard...it is possible that the Shogunate managed to exist only because of how tightly woven the Lunars had made the people of the Solar Empire. The world was shattered with titanic battles, and the Dragonborn fought with the Solars and Lunars for years...and yet, when they returned, they found that society had been chugging along without them as best as they could, rather than dissolving into all out anarchy that would have completely shattered the Blessed Isle as a base of power.<br /> <br /> <b>The Silver Pact</b><br /> Unfortunately, this is easily explained as being the result of the Elder Lunars. Of all the mortals in all of Creation...the Lunars are the only ones still alive who lost all the glories that were theirs. The Terrestrials of the Usurpation are long dead. No Solars survived it. And the Sidereals still have Yu Shan. No one is more keenly aware of how far the world has fallen than the Lunar Elders who lived through it, and no one has lost nearly as much. That, coupled with the Breaking of the Bond (whatever that is), along with a probably dose of untreated PTSD had probably led the Lunar Elders into hating the Dragonblooded with an unrivaled passion...and possibly drove some of them at least a little bit mad.<br /> <br /> So, along comes a newly Exalted Lunar, who just got rescued from a bunch of angry Dragonblooded screaming &quot;Die, foul Anathema!&quot; and brought out to one of the domains of the Lunars. They are new to their power, and an Elder Lunar speaks to them and offers to protect them and train them until they are ready to go back out to make their own way. Often, such a Lunar may accept such a generous offer...and then spends the rest of their time training with this Lunar hearing of the atrocities of the Dragonblooded and the Sidereals...and tales of the First Age...and takes part in the Elder's schemes to cast down the Realm because, well, the Elder is their mentor.<br /> <br /> Then, when the day comes that it is time for them to go their own way...well, they have been so well taught on the evils of the Dragonblooded and the necessity of destroying the Realm, that they now believe it to be true. And if the time comes that they take on a mentee, they too will tell stories passed down to them from their mentor, and speak of the evils of the Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> So, perhaps the 'chains' that the Lunars need to throw off are actually the Elders, and the passed-down hate the Elders have for the ones who took everything from them. Perhaps the Silver Pact is actually Silver Chains binding the Chosen of Luna into a path of destruction. Perhaps it is time to stop fighting their ancestors' war. Perhaps it is time to do something better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:07:27-07:00","id":736415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=734820#post734820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what Smiles is saying is that &quot;I can reshape the world with my third circle sorcery&quot; of the Solars and the &quot;my day to day job is to keep the laws of nature and causality working and I know all loopholes to exploit them&quot; of the Sidereals is much more goal-oriented than the Lunars &quot;well, I can shapechange and ... uh ... was around in the last age too. Yay me?&quot;. The Lunars have a unique tool but the only thing they seem to use it for is totally reactive - destroy the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what Smiles was saying. It still comes down to preconceptions and assumptions lowballing what could potentially be much more grand. You say that shapeshifting is limited, and that Lunars are reactive; I say that Lunars make living next to a Dominion like a horror movie for the Dynasts with the misfortune to be assigned to such a post. Lights get snuffed out, communication with your fellows is cut off, and you're so very, very alone. You'll feel it even harder, given where the true might of the Dragon-Blooded comes from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars are desperately in need of something they can actively do. All human societies, without any exception, and in fact all forms of life are hardwired to preserve and better themselves. Making Lunars to mere rage-fulled warriors makes them kind of unrealistic. They need to be able to build and enhance stuff, both literally and metaphorically - and just because they are animal-inspired doesn't change that. Over at rpg.net I once suggested a charm called &quot;Million Souls Home&quot; which allows them to instinctively build working homes and infrastructure for lots of people ... as do termites. </div> </div> </div>That's not quite on par with the animal legendry which their Charms use as a bedrock. It's about the awe, especially terrified awe, of people coming in from the wilderness with lurid tales of weird and frightening feats which the beasts performed. Cats and owls that stood and watched just outside of a village by someone who drops dead of illness or infirmity, suggesting that they know who's going to die. Armored terrors that can snap a coaster in half in one bite and turn steel with their hide. Tigers that seem to emerge from locales that couldn't hide them. Long-necked, whip-tailed and more elephantine than an elephant dinosaurs, their hide fearsome and barbed, their tails capable of tearing the divine ichor from gods and demons and resounding louder than thunder when they strike. While I like to work in a lot of real life nuances myself, Lunars revel in the spirit of unsettling and frightening others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars should be able to create a highly effective but subconsciously working learning-by-imitation/play strategy for people, like a cat-mother bringing half-dead mice to her kittens. They should be able to whalesing helpful or manipulative memes into existence which pop up at the same time in multiple, far away places. They should be able to slowly, passively but irreversibely make their surrounding more supportive to life - not like a Solar plopping down a palace via sorcerous working, but like the roots of a tree slowly breaking and eroding stone to fertile earth.<br /> <br /> And besides something they can actively do, Lunars need something great they have actively DONE. Mate and companion to Solars is ok and fine - but at the moment they look more like trophy wives. There is no problem at all with being the minor half of a legendary pair, if it's done right: Enkidu was never as protagonist-y as Gilgamesh, but the story had enough points to make Enkidu a vital part of the story. Lunars are missing something like that when the game talks about the age when the celestial exalted still ruled Creation. The Solar ruled and created wonders, the Sidereals kept the world running and do so today. And the Lunars ... well ... most likely they helped to rule the world? Or built some smaller wonders? Maybe? </div> </div> </div>They have done something great - they locked horns with a civilization that had those vaunted masters of fate and the children of the five dragons, who had all those warstriders and flying ships, and they've made that civilization bleed pale and clear. Grand tales of overwhelming victory might get included in the Lunar book, to show how the undying hope and rage of the Lunars is putting them ahead in the long game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:40:28-07:00","id":736463,"title":"","content":"Taliesin and Anteros got it pretty good.<br /> <br /> The Lunars need to have had an actual <b>impact</b> on history. In virtually all versions the Lunars have been a footnote. Standing up to someone is impressive but people only remember you if you win and the Lunars have seemingly never won. The Solars won. The Sidereals won. The Dragon-blooded won. And <b>that </b>is what history recorded. An extraneous exalted.<br /> It's not enough to make your enemy bleed. For history to truly remember you, your enemy has to die.<br /> <br /> I didn't say that shapeshifting wasn't impressive, I said it wasn't on par with; <b>PHENOMINAL COSMIC POWERRRRR!!!!!!!!</b> The Solars and Sidereals have that. The Behemoth you describe is a massive, frightening, devastating and powerful juggernaut. But the Solars killed Juggernaut. MoW is using his corpse as a castle. A Behemoth isn't a miracle, its just a monster.<br /> <br /> We're not trying to downplay Lunars, we feel that they've <i>been</i> downplayed. And the fact that we-erm, Lunars have had as much screentime in the Core Book as the Liminals and less than everyone else. That isn't filling us with hope.<br /> <br /> <i>(also, raise your hand if you said; &quot;itty bitty living space.&quot; you know where)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:46:28-07:00","id":736478,"title":"","content":"@ Saur Ops Specialist<br /> <br /> I never said that shapeshifting is limited either. I just said that shapeshifting is a tool, but not a goal. It doesn't matter if shapeshifting is werewhatever-only or something that includes other states of being and the most fantastical chimerical creatures, there is still the question &quot;what are you going to do with that?&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's what I mean with &quot;reactive&quot;. The Lunars want to tear down the Realm and fight the Dragonblooded and Sidereals.<br /> Fine. Ok. And then? What are they going to do when they succeed? Run to the countryside, hide in bushes and jump at mortals, screaming loud &quot;BOOOO!&quot; when one comes along - if making people afraid and creeping them out is so important to them as you say, this sounds like a reasonable endgame.<br /> <br /> For me this sounds just lacking. Currently the Lunars seem to be defined almost completely by their opposition to something else, but they have no clear goal or even options about what they want to do on their own, no higher goals or own aspirations (contrary to their current state of &quot;we don't want that these guys over there reach their goals of ruling the world&quot;).<br /> The Lunars should be the strongest Exalted in the setting after the Solars disappeared - but strangely the thought of &quot;we are the top dog, so we should rule creation&quot; never seemed to pop up and all they got is &quot;well, let's find some barbarian tribe so they can worship us&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's what I wanted to say with my charm ideas: generative or protective charms and powers work on their own, destructive effects work just when there is someone or something that needs to be destroyed. If Lunars don't get the first type of charm, their stories are limited to &quot;defeat enemy&quot; but they won't be able to tell stories about &quot;create and manage kingdom&quot; because they don't have the means for this (or just the means a normal human would have for that).<br /> That's why I liked the 1000 Stream Rivers so much. Ok, I admit, the execution of the idea was not really overwhelmingly good in Ex2, but the theory behind it was awesome. The Lunars just need more abilities that interact with such a goal.<br /> <br /> Luckily the devs said in the corebook and in some older forum posts something like &quot;the Lunars of today are no longer the Lunars of the First Age and they changed themselves&quot;. Which is at least for me and my group enough reason to allow our Lunar to completely rewrite his charmset from rage-filled warform-smash warrior to something much more subtle, creative and less destruction-focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:55:40-07:00","id":736492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=736463#post736463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taliesin and Anteros got it pretty good.<br /> <br /> The Lunars need to have had an actual <b>impact</b> on history. In virtually all versions the Lunars have been a footnote. Standing up to someone is impressive but people only remember you if you win and the Lunars have seemingly never won. The Solars won. The Sidereals won. The Dragon-blooded won. And <b>that </b>is what history recorded. An extraneous exalted.<br /> It's not enough to make your enemy bleed. For history to truly remember you, your enemy has to die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars fired up the decline of the Shogunate. With the Empress gone, they'll step up the downfall of the Realm. Then they'll become something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't say that shapeshifting wasn't impressive, I said it wasn't on par with; <b>PHENOMINAL COSMIC POWERRRRR!!!!!!!!</b> The Solars and Sidereals have that. The Behemoth you describe is a massive, frightening, devastating and powerful juggernaut. But the Solars killed Juggernaut. MoW is using his corpse as a castle. A Behemoth isn't a miracle, its just a monster. </div> </div> </div>First thing, downplaying it is definitely another form of saying that it's not impressive. Secondly, scrub everything you know about Juggernaut, because its life, death-ish circumstances and such aren't getting put under a microscope or attributed to Solars. Third, Juggernaut's corpse could be revived, and the Mask finds this possibility unsettling at best. Some unknown being of great power and courage cacked the behemoth; trying to do it again might just be out of the league of anyone alive... or dead, for that matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're not trying to downplay Lunars, we feel that they've <i>been</i> downplayed. And the fact that we-erm, Lunars have had as much screentime in the Core Book as the Liminals and less than everyone else. That isn't filling us with hope.<br /> <br /> <i>(also, raise your hand if you said; &quot;itty bitty living space.&quot; you know where)</i> </div> </div> </div>Lots of people downplay the concept of werewolves, too. WW happened to do something way more substantial than the expected &quot;you wake up with someone's blood on you and they're dead/chained in your own basement like you do every full moon&quot; with them a long time ago. Just saying.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T19:00:41-07:00","id":736498,"title":"","content":"As with most rebel forces, I imagine they have a variety of ideas of what they want after the Realm.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I really wouldn't\u200b judge too much on like a paragraph or two in the Core book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T19:03:23-07:00","id":736500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=736498#post736498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with most rebel forces, I imagine they have a variety of ideas of what they want after the Realm.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I really wouldn't\u200b judge too much on like a paragraph or two in the Core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a finite limit to how active you can be when you're no longer the military, but rather the resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T19:05:37-07:00","id":736504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=736478#post736478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Saur Ops Specialist<br /> <br /> The Lunars should be the strongest Exalted in the setting after the Solars disappeared - but strangely the thought of &quot;we are the top dog, so we should rule creation&quot; never seemed to pop up and all they got is &quot;well, let's find some barbarian tribe so they can worship us&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they should not. The Dragon-Blooded are the strongest Exalted in the setting, because there are thousands of them and all of Creation's peoples serve them. It would do a horrendous disservice to the power of the Terrestrial Exalted if the Lunars just rocked up, pushed over their puny little Realm despite being outnumbered hundreds to one and declared themselves rulers of all Creation. And of course they want to do that, it's absurd to think that they've never even considered taking over Creation when all of their effort since the fall of the First Age has been dedicated towards taking over Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T19:16:06-07:00","id":736524,"title":"","content":"I've nothing specific to add to Saur Ops' points, so suffice to say that I agree with everything he's saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T19:17:01-07:00","id":736525,"title":"","content":"Obviously I went by personal strength and not numbers. After all, this is a game where heroes take on enemies or armies much stronger than them and win.<br /> <br /> But if you take your approach and go just by numbers, then the Dragon-Blooded are also much stronger than the Solars. But strangely for Solars &quot;take over the world&quot; seems to be a viable goal, while Lunars seem to have the meta-knowledge of their non-protagonism and so have only &quot;take over some backwater tribe in Creations asscrack&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T19:48:03-07:00","id":736566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=736525#post736525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously I went by personal strength and not numbers. After all, this is a game where heroes take on enemies or armies much stronger than them and win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted is a game where you can take on armies of <i>mortals</i>. Celestials being able to take on armies of <i>Dragon-Blooded</i>, to the extent that it was possible in previous editions, was incredibly terrible and did nothing but make the Terrestrials look like useless chumps. And thankfully 3e has done away with it altogether. I mean seriously, are you arguing with a straight face that Lunars are made to look bad because they haven't single-handedly fought and killed a hundred Dragon-Blooded each and their hundreds of thousands of mortals?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=736525#post736525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you take your approach and go just by numbers, then the Dragon-Blooded are also much stronger than the Solars. But strangely for Solars &quot;take over the world&quot; seems to be a viable goal, while Lunars seem to have the meta-knowledge of their non-protagonism and so have only &quot;take over some backwater tribe in Creations asscrack&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not how they're portrayed at all. They've taken over a large continent that's of great spiritual and economic significance to the Realm, and they have large dominions elsewhere in Creation where the Realm's legions dare not tread. And let's not forget this was happening while the Realm's power was at its peak. There were Solars around then too, and their failure to do anything was so total that they aren't even mentioned, while the Lunars were still taking on the might of the Realm's legions and winning. Not winning every time, no, but if that's what you require to consider someone a useful protagonist then you have hugely overinflated expectations. I also find it ridiculous to look at all these examples of the Lunars <i>actually taking over large chunks of the world</i>, and the precisely zero examples of Solars doing the same, and then claim that the Lunars are somehow shown as not capable of taking over the world while the Solars are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T19:53:19-07:00","id":736607,"title":"","content":"I wish to say that Lanaya is also talking sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:09:22-07:00","id":736637,"title":"","content":"I don't quite think that <i>blatant </i>PHENOMENAL COSMIC POWER quite suits the Lunars - the same way Luna doesn't have a singular thing that can be said to be exceedingly standout the way the Unconquered Sun has his undefeated perfection or the Maidens have Fate -, which doesn't make them any less suitable of being considered Celestial Exalts - or Luna any less of an Incarna. In my view, they are the power of the heavens on Creation incarnate in its most primal, yet most subtle form.<br /> <br /> They have unmatched flexibility and guile among the celestial exalted, and wield both sorcery and martial arts that reach the height of divine power, even if they may never breach their highest secrets. Their bodies and raw capabilities express incredible power beyond the Solars and Sidereals, even if their respective world-shifting prowess and reality-ordering finesse are beyond Luna's Chosen. Through their shapeshifting and their link to animals, they are the closest to the natural world, and through their keen sensitivity and their ancient discenment, may understand it and its cycles better than even the dragonblood, attuned to the elements themselves, ever could.<br /> <br /> I agree that they could use a lasting mark on Creation or an impressive constructive proof of their feats, but at the same time that might be the sort of thing that would lessen their narrative and take away from their role in Creation now - their vicious underdog role as defined by the Usurpation and their bitter, centuries long inherited grudge that they nonetheless have the potential to break free from. But I don't think the writers are going to ONLY use that for the Lunars, and I certainly don't think they're going to be reduced to mere rage filled warriors; their conflict, even individually, is more nuanced than that and has a lot more meaning for them <i>and</i> for the rest of Creation.<br /> <br /> And there was something they actively did. They did have an important, powerful place in the First Age: where the Solars ruled and created wonders, and the Sidereals ordained and maintained the world, the Lunars guarded it. They were the wardens of the Old Realm, and the protectors of the world, but as the Moon seems faint by comparison when the Sun is still in the sky, so too does the significance of the Lunars of then seem small. But when your duty leaves you outside the center of the greatest accomplishments of your time and you are by designation placed as a complimentary second to another, of course your achievements enhance the brilliance of those who have occupied the stage rather than be recognized on their own. The Lunars worked to support the Solars in all things and labored away from sight in a way different from the Sidereals, and a consequence of that is that their shine wouldn't get through all else that was more evident of the essence of that era. Without them, the Old Realm may well not have been near as successful, and the amazing creations of the Solars would not have come into being so easily, but the Lunars kept at their functions at a distance which made them easy to overlook.<br /> <br /> P.S.: And of course more was posted while I was writing that. Nonetheless, I agree with Saur and Lanaya's points too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 10-28-2015, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:16:46-07:00","id":736650,"title":"","content":"I think it should also be pointed out that people do not play Solar Exalted for Solar Circle Sorcery.<br /> <br /> <i>Some</i> <i>individuals</i> play Solar Exalted who are sorcerors of the Solar Circle. Many individuals do not. Solar Circle Sorcery is merely part of the holistic package of Solarness that appeals to Solar players.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, everyone who wants to play the canonical Lunar Exalted wants to play a skinwalker, facestealer, or werebeast of some kind. Because if they didn't, they'd play a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:26:40-07:00","id":736661,"title":"","content":"An important point that hasn't been discussed yet is what tearing down the Realm means.<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean launching terror attacks on the Blessed Isle, or trying to turn civilians against the government by telling them Lunar schemes can't melt jade beams.<br /> (I mean, for most Lunars anyway. Some Lunars are terrible!)<br /> <br /> For most Lunars, it means that soldiers are going to burn down your friend's village, and you burn their barracks the night before they can march. Or you roll up up on a House Cynis plantation to lead a slave revolt. Or you overthrow the satrap who's doing terrible things to your city in favor of a system of government you and a circle of local intellectuals thought up.<br /> <br /> 3E's Realm embodies everything that was wrong with colonialism. The Silver Pact is <i>the </i>anti-colonialist faction in the book. Here as in the real world, the point is to replace oppression with a kinder system, not to burn everything down and then shrug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/832-surlyseraph","name":"SurlySeraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:40:59-07:00","id":736679,"title":"","content":"I really think that rather than downplaying Luunars we're merely pointing out what appears to be obvious flaws or weakness in the way they're shown.<br /> Most Exalted had a clear reason for being, a role that only they could fill, a specific purpose nobody was as qualified to accomplish, except for Lunars. When I say this, I'm not downplaying them, just pointing that they weren't given their own niche to fill.<br /> <br /> We get a description of the Silver Pact raising up barbarian armies to harass the Realm forces, getting the tribes defeated, then moving on to start again, eroding the Realm's strength. What other group is given such a narrow focus and fixed modus operandi?<br /> We're told not all Lunars get on this train, but no other major Lunar faction is mentioned, when even the Siddies being divided between Bronze, Gold, followers of the Sleepwalker is explicitely stated. And they're three times less numerous! We're not back to the point of being told to pick different weapons to be able to differentiate between Lunars, but the narrow focus is clearly felt nonetheless.<br /> Pointing his out is not downplaying Lunars, just attracting notice on the perception I have of this fact.<br /> <br /> As for the shapeshifting thing, in earlier editions Lunar shapeshifting was designed to be &quot;primal&quot; or whatever, rather than esoteric. They didn't turn into strange creatures with wondrous abilities, they became animals, sometimes in giant or miniature versions. It's a design choice. It's not a bad one, but there is no way turning into Zilla (not even Godzilla) would rival SCS or SMA.<br /> 3e looks like it will go even more into the animal thing, what with Luna making her Chosen bestial because of Gaia. There are ways to make this more than just about turning into giant critters, so I hope we'll see something less limited this time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T21:12:47-07:00","id":736780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=733513#post733513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reason that Terrestrials can manage to fight them, and have kept them away, is because the Terrestrials are leaning on relics of the Jack Kirby wonderland, and more of those objects of power are lost or ruined with each passing year. Eventually, the combined orchestration of Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded will fall before the Lunars, because the Lunars don't need the legacy of the Solars to defeat their foes, if their foes don't have it any more, either.<br /> <br /> That's been the stated direction for years, now. The link to most of the material describing it is near the start of the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I hope you're wrong about that. Because that really makes Lunars, Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals into massive chumps. Under that assumption, Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals are chumps because apparently the only reason they can sit at the table at all is because they have Solar guns. And it makes the Lunars chumps because two of their main antagonists are only worthwhile because they have Solar guns, and what does that say about Lunars?<br /> <br /> 'Salright for Solars, I suppose. They get to be the only ones who actually matter in the setting for a third edition running.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T21:29:48-07:00","id":736846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=736780#post736780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, I hope you're wrong about that. Because that really makes Lunars, Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals into massive chumps. Under that assumption, Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals are chumps because apparently the only reason they can sit at the table at all is because they have Solar guns. And it makes the Lunars chumps because two of their main antagonists are only worthwhile because they have Solar guns, and what does that say about Lunars?<br /> <br /> 'Salright for Solars, I suppose. They get to be the only ones who actually matter in the setting for a third edition running.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarification: It would have taken the Lunars a while to whittle the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals down, but it would have been done by now if they weren't sitting on giant piles of First Age magic. Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals in that setup wouldn't have been able to mass attacks on Lunar strongholds nearly so easily, allowing much larger and longer-lasting Dominions to cause much greater losses to their opposition. When infrastructure is gone and crumbling and there's little chance for Dragon-Blooded or Sidereals to acquire powerful daiklaves and such, the advantage goes to Lunars, because they basically have a built-in set of Evocations in Deadly Beastman Transformation, kind of (it's projected to be balanced off of not being able to use Evocations, so it's likely on par-ish with them).<br /> <br /> Better? That was my actual intent; there's no way a giant conflict like that is going to be done quickly, but between the Usurpation and RY 768 is somewhere between thirteen and fifteen centuries, which would have been ample time for Lunars to mop up Terrestrials and Sidereals that are struggling to stay armed with non-Artifact weapons and protected with sheets of hide and/or mail, and the rest of the world is practically in the stone age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T23:17:32-07:00","id":737073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=736780#post736780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it makes the Lunars chumps because two of their main antagonists are only worthwhile because they have Solar guns, and what does that say about Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, if it takes a literal army of the Exalts meant to be soldiers, armed with a mountain of first age solar magic and backed by the 'manipulate Fate&quot; exalts to pose a credible threat to Lunars, that's not Lunars being <i>chumps</i>.<br /> <br /> That's lunars being <b><i>fucking</i> awesome.</b> If the Realm absolutely needs all of that First Age Solar stuff to pose a threat to the Lunars, that that tells me that Lunars are badasses that it takes weapons made by first age Solars to fight.<br /> <br /> If magic weapons made by the most skilled sorcerers and craftsmen in millennia, wielded by exalted soldiers, are what it takes to fight the Lunars and actually pose a plausible threat, then Lunars are implicitly equal to the Solars.<br /> <br /> In this setting, that's the <i>opposite</i> of being a chump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T00:18:35-07:00","id":737229,"title":"","content":"So, 3rd Edition seems to be getting back to the 1st Edition setting, more or less, which had a good premise the books seemed intent on not getting through.<br /> <br /> See, the most terrifyingly powerful thing in Exalted is the Realm. Nothing else comes close. It is Ten Thousand Dragons. Ten Thousand EXALTED. The Realm has people like Cathak Cainan, Peleps Aramida, and Tepet Arada. Even though Arada left, the other two did not, and it is noted that he is one of the best, but not THE only one. It has people like Ragara Bagwei, Mnemon and Cynis Mond, and even though the first and third are away from Realm politics, they do believe in the Realm, they did work for its betterment, and you can be damn sure they will show up like Gandalf in Helm's Deep if your anathema army is crossing the sea. It has immaculate monks with multiple anathema kills like Peleps Deled, Imminent Thunder, and Ragara Myrrun. Each one a beacon of celestial-defying might.<br /> <br /> And all of them are decked from head to toe in the panoply of ages gone by and a world bled dry.<br /> <br /> Remember the special caveat of Artifact 5, in previous editions? How you have access to their arsenal of wonders? Grand airships flying the sky and raining lightning death upon the ground below. Immense statues of obsidian that breathe out molten light. Thousand-Forged Dragons. Grand Warstriders whose Evocations can glass entire cities. All that is within the vaults of the Dynasty. All that can be pulled out if the need is great enough, if you can just convince them, at that level, to give you the keys to chariots pulled by palace-trampling bronze bulls and armor of brass that turns men into gods of war.<br /> <br /> And all of that does not take the Sidereals into account.<br /> <br /> We are talking about sixty-plus of them. The majority faction. The HEGEMONY. The Bronze Faction. Including the single most powerful Exalted alive, in political and personal terms, Chejop Kejack. Including the most terrifying martial artist alive, Anys Syn. We are talking about the people currently ruling Heaven. The people whom the politics are working FOR. The people who get to have the lion's share of the resources, of the projects, of the allies. The ones who get the first pick at Starmetal, the ones who get all the best toys. The ones under the wings of the powers. And they are aware. Their entire plan IS The Realm. Every day, they look at it, they strengthen it, they fight for it. Sixty-plus Celestial Exalted with Heaven on their pocket, and they are dedicated into preserving, fighting for, and fighting with, this might.<br /> <br /> And with them, there's the Gods<br /> <br /> You know, the Imperial City has a God. He is incredibly powerful, wealthy, and loves the Empire. The Empire itself. All the gods of things the Empire loves, and furthers, such as Imperial Might, Rulership, Order, Cities, Trade, Dominance. They are the hegemony, and those thriving under this hegemony are powerful Gods indeed. Those who decided to play with the Immaculate Order rather than to raise grand cults may not receive power like the Great Forks and Whitewall Lords... but those who did it since the beginning and are tied to the machinery of it have quite a bit of power, and they will protect that which empowers them.<br /> <br /> And then, there's the weird.<br /> <br /> We know there is a Legion made out of Mountain Folk. And while they are being entirely reworked, their status as a Realm Tributary is not something noted as changing. There are Exigents noted as being on the side of the Realm, and in the what we know, it is noted they are part of the makeup of Wyld Hunts. There might be a Faerie-Queen enamored of a Dynastic lord, her hobgoblins serving the Empire (despite the stigma against that extant after what Cevis Ghandarva did); and... likely much more strange things like the Mountain Folk. They rule Creation, and Creation is strange. Above and beyond the automatons mentioned above, weird folks with strange powers live in Creation, and the majority of them will give the Realm some token of their power.<br /> <br /> All that is the Realm. When united, it is the single most powerful thing extant. Return of the Scarlet Empress is a terrible book that worfs the entire rest of the setting, even THAT atrocity had to kill all Sidereals and destabilize the Realm before the Yozi came out, because, that sword described above? It would cleave the Ebon Dragon in half if its edge hadn't been dulled. It is the closest thing to the mighty Exalted Host of old to currently exist. It is terrifying.<br /> <br /> And the existence of the Caul means it FAILED.<br /> <br /> Quoth the old man:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejack, Exalted Third Edition Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars\u2014the most numerous; one of the most dangerous<br /> as well. He was keenly aware of the Full Moons out<br /> there doing who-knows-what, maneuvering for some<br /> plan hidden even from Kejak\u2019s eyes. They were hidden<br /> in the West, too, there on the Caul. The Caul had held so<br /> much promise in the wake of the Usurpation, but all those<br /> halcyon dreams had come to ash and blood along with<br /> the rest of the age, and now they were at the brink of a<br /> war that would send even more cracks through the fabric<br /> of his Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>He wanted nothing more than to have The Caul. All that sword described above came down upon it.<br /> <br /> They failed.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi took over his Nameless Lair. You know what this means?<br /> <br /> It means Lookshy and The Realm, both at the height of their power, utterly failed to stop him. And they have to have tried. They have to have done their best.<br /> <br /> They lost.<br /> <br /> Raksi took over Sperimim. SPERIMIM! Capital of all learning, the place that holds the Book of Three Circles. It is priceless. It is something all those powers would wish. And she took it. And nobody will take from her. Nobody dares to approach her.<br /> <br /> The Lunars were driven from the world, when they were Usurped with the Solars. And each step they took was fighting the most powerful empire in Creation, and winning, step by step. That? Is something that the hunted, reincarnating Solars utterly failed at. Joachim, if he was indeed a Solar, may have made quite a splash, but he was still brought down. No Solars created dominions, none were ever able to survive its onslaught of power.<br /> <br /> That? Is not something a Solar in the Time of Tumult will ever be able to replicate. Because everything is now falling down.<br /> <br /> It was asked many times in this thread what is their victory, and what they did that is worthy of being Celestial. They looked upon the greatest might in the setting, and slowly, but inexorably, pushed it back. Something the reincarnating Solars weren't able to do. If you don't think that's impressive, or worthy of Celestial Might, you weren't paying attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T01:18:14-07:00","id":737343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=737229#post737229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Solars created dominions, none were ever able to survive its onslaught of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that's largely because until the disappearance of the Empress, the reaction to one of those rare Solars showing up was far more focused and determined than the reaction to <i>yet another</i> Lunar showing up.<br /> <br /> <br /> But my favourite quote is still...<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 106</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cTen thousand dragons rule the world,\u201d goes the chant of the Realm\u2019s military cadets. Ten thousand claws and fangs encircle that world at the behest of the Silver Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars don't have their single, unified empire. That's not their style. They have some dominions - the Caul being the most well-known - but those are the exception.<br /> Instead, they turned the threshold into what amounts to a giant source of environemental damage for the realm. It's a death of a thousand cuts.<br /> <br /> And then there's the occasional attempts at just killing the Empress - the second point on the list of &quot;what could have caused her disappearance&quot; is &quot;<i>Lunars happened</i>&quot;.<br /> Because apparently, they are even active on the Blessed Isle. If they attempted to kill the Empress - likely the most well-guarded person in all of creation - three times over the last three centuries and actually managed to get close to succeeding... how many <i>other</i>, less well-guarded dynasts fell to them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T01:48:01-07:00","id":737375,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I liked that bit, showing they're active in the Realm. I mean, with their shapeshifting, assassinating major figures in the Realm is certainly feasible for the Realm.<br /> <br /> (In my game, the Lunars killed her to weaken the Realm prior to invasion. It didn't come up directly in the game though, just indirectly.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T02:25:13-07:00","id":737445,"title":"","content":"Thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) I don't think it's very interesting if it's so pat, and so solved that we can say &quot;Oh, well. The Dragonblooded and the Sidereals have access to First Age magic. If they didn't, the Lunars would definitely have taken them&quot;. Surely it's worthwhile for Lunars to target DB assets, but it doesn't seem very interesting if that's the *only* reason a Dragonblooded Empire could stand against the Lunars, or even a decisive one, or if we can call it that easily. I think if we had a reverse situation where the Sidereals and Dragonblooded were somehow dispossessed and the Lunars were a power with greater access to First Age magic, it would be grindingly challenging for the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> 2) While Colapso's description of the pulp fantasy might of the Empire of Granbretan and Melnibone... sorry, the Realm (this is Exalted and the Realm and not a Moorcock Ysyr esqye sorcerous empire, I was forgetting myself) is fairly cool, I'm pretty sure in 1e they were not talked on in terms of having such an arsenal of forgotten First Age might to bring to the table (is this how the campaigns against the Bull of the North were discussed, for instane?). In 1e I think it was the case that the reason they hold ground against the Lunars is that mainly, the Legions will fuck you up. Just the Legions. No skyships, no might First Age weapons. Just Legions (and the Navy). There's the might First Age Defense Grid, but the Empress calls this only out in extremis.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Realm will change in 3e, since it is apparently now with 300% more plunder (including First Age booty) and many, many more mentions of their &quot;boot&quot; and their &quot;heel&quot;. <br /> <br /> (Contrast the 1e &quot;The Scarlet Throne enforced its rule by making it more expensive to refuse the Realm than appease it. The Empress demanded only moderate payment from her tributaries and was swift to dispatch her legions to protect her vassals. Her tendency to sent those same legions to rearrange local governments at the first sign of disloyalty resolved any lingering doubts her vassals may have had&quot; with what the 3e core gives, which for one excerpt is &quot;The Realm has accomplished all this through a policy of ruthless expansion and unhesitating force aimed at any who would gainsay it. The Wyld Hunt pursues any hint of the Anathema in the Realm\u2019s holdings. The Legions crush any organized military resistance to the Empress\u2019s will.&quot;. Tonally almost totally different, right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T06:28:01-07:00","id":737904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=736846#post736846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better? That was my actual intent; there's no way a giant conflict like that is going to be done quickly, but between the Usurpation and RY 768 is somewhere between thirteen and fifteen centuries, which would have been ample time for Lunars to mop up Terrestrials and Sidereals that are struggling to stay armed with non-Artifact weapons and protected with sheets of hide and/or mail, and the rest of the world is practically in the stone age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better, but I still think it's not so cut and dried. Exalted 3e is supposed to be the edition where we can't just look at the belligerents involved and call the fight with almost perfect accuracy because there's a strict power hierarchy, after all. And, as Ghosthead said, it's pretty damn boring if you can look at the situation and say &quot;Take away the Solar guns and the Sidereals/Dragon-Blood lose, do not pass Go, do not collect $200.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now I'm not saying that Solar guns aren't an advantage, and probably a big one. But they shouldn't be the ONLY reason that the conflict is still ongoing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=737073#post737073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, if it takes a literal army of the Exalts meant to be soldiers, armed with a mountain of first age solar magic and backed by the 'manipulate Fate&quot; exalts to pose a credible threat to Lunars, that's not Lunars being <i>chumps</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, essentially, that wasn't the scenario I was responding to. Essentially, the scenario wasn't &quot;Sidereals and Realm Dragon-Blooded vs. Lunars.&quot; It was &quot;People with Solar guns vs. Lunars.&quot; That's chumping for everyone involved because it sells Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals extremely short while implying they're basically worthless on their own, and it sells the Lunars short because...well, those are their two main enemeies, the ones about which a great deal of time, effort and book space is devoted, and as soon as you destroy their tech tree they fold like one of those newer maps.<br /> <br /> To put it another way...how shit would the Star Wars movies have been if the ONLY thing the Empire had going for it was the Death Star? (My answer is pretty shit)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T07:18:05-07:00","id":738116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=737904#post737904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;People with Solar guns vs. Lunars.&quot; That's chumping for everyone involved because it sells Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals extremely short while implying they're basically worthless on their own, and it sells the Lunars short because...</div> </div> </div> </div>And I read this, and I dnon't understand it.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that I believe that the realm and the sids need Solar weapons, but if they <i>do </i>need Solar made weapons, then that makes Lunars the opposites of Chumps.<br /> <br /> If I'm a Lunar warrior fighting against the realm, and the Dragonblooded Soldiers and the Wyld Hunts, and the Immaculate Masters(or their equivelents) all need to be wielding artifact weapons that were forged by the greatest craftsmen in millenia and equipped with magic woven by the greatest sorcerers in millenia, just to pose a credible threat to me and my buddies, I certainly don' feel like a Chump. I feel like a major badass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:10:44-07:00","id":738745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=736679#post736679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think that rather than downplaying Luunars we're merely pointing out what appears to be obvious flaws or weakness in the way they're shown.<br /> Most Exalted had a clear reason for being, a role that only they could fill, a specific purpose nobody was as qualified to accomplish, except for Lunars. When I say this, I'm not downplaying them, just pointing that they weren't given their own niche to fill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not why any of the Exalted were created, in setting.<br /> <br /> Each of the seven Incarnae and the five Elemental Dragons made Exaltations because all of them wanted to support the war effort against the Primordials, and each one created only the kind of Exalted that was possible for them to create. That each Host <i>could</i> fulfill particular roles was more of a happy accident.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun wanted to create leaders for mankind and the very best of the best, because that's just the kind of god he is. But his goal wasn't to create an entire Host of Solar Circle sorcerors, and not every single Solar becomes a Solar Circle sorceror.<br /> <br /> Luna wanted to elevate and empower her own particular kind of heroes, but that doesn't mean she intended them to have any kind of specific, unique role in the world. Or at least, not the kind that comes with or necessitates fancy powers like Solar Circle sorcery, Sidereal Astrology, or breeding more Exaltations.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's also not why the Exalted were created, out of setting.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted are meant to let us play werewolves, skinwalkers, and face-stealers. First Edition didn't do that right, because First Edition didn't know its own mechanics. Second Edition tried to do something else by throwing in lots of Wyld stuff and turning into anything but animals. Third Edition is going back to First Edition's simplicity, but with two editions' worth of mechanical and narrative mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:15:52-07:00","id":739253,"title":"","content":"RE: Ghosthead, point number 2 - Dace's account of a fight against a Realm-supported monarch in the Dawnbook of early 1e had said monarch equipped with a staff that could call storms and lightning, supplied by the Realm to help her prop up her rule. That's what they were willing to give to a mortal; imagine what they're keeping for themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=737904#post737904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better, but I still think it's not so cut and dried. Exalted 3e is supposed to be the edition where we can't just look at the belligerents involved and call the fight with almost perfect accuracy because there's a strict power hierarchy, after all. And, as Ghosthead said, it's pretty damn boring if you can look at the situation and say &quot;Take away the Solar guns and the Sidereals/Dragon-Blood lose, do not pass Go, do not collect $200.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now I'm not saying that Solar guns aren't an advantage, and probably a big one. But they shouldn't be the ONLY reason that the conflict is still ongoing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just talked a hypothetical scenario taking place over centuries worth of time with an extreme advantage in the Lunar corner. That's not being cut and dried; that's a long, bloody war where the advantage ultimately but only after great effort means victory. Of course, the Lunars could also strike at the most vulnerable points of Dragon-Blooded and Sidereal existence, as both Exaltations are set from birth and all, and killing one means either that they have to start over, or that you're down one more potential branch on the family of the dragon-heroes. That would likely get things done a lot faster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, essentially, that wasn't the scenario I was responding to. Essentially, the scenario wasn't &quot;Sidereals and Realm Dragon-Blooded vs. Lunars.&quot; It was &quot;People with Solar guns vs. Lunars.&quot; That's chumping for everyone involved because it sells Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals extremely short while implying they're basically worthless on their own, and it sells the Lunars short because...well, those are their two main enemeies, the ones about which a great deal of time, effort and book space is devoted, and as soon as you destroy their tech tree they fold like one of those newer maps.<br /> <br /> To put it another way...how shit would the Star Wars movies have been if the ONLY thing the Empire had going for it was the Death Star? (My answer is pretty shit)<br /> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals get way more out of infrastructure than Lunars do. They can freely stack their Evocations on their most powerful capabilities, whereas Lunars have a sideways shift from DBT to whatever Evocations they have, but not both. So, it is, in fact, quite important to note Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded with this armory against the Lunars with damn near nothing, because any other group might not have those same layer-able advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:05:15-07:00","id":739402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=738745#post738745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that's not why any of the Exalted were created, in setting.<br /> <br /> Each of the seven Incarnae and the five Elemental Dragons made Exaltations because all of them wanted to support the war effort against the Primordials, and each one created only the kind of Exalted that was possible for them to create. That each Host <i>could</i> fulfill particular roles was more of a happy accident.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun wanted to create leaders for mankind and the very best of the best, because that's just the kind of god he is. But his goal wasn't to create an entire Host of Solar Circle sorcerors, and not every single Solar becomes a Solar Circle sorceror.<br /> <br /> Luna wanted to elevate and empower her own particular kind of heroes, but that doesn't mean she intended them to have any kind of specific, unique role in the world. Or at least, not the kind that comes with or necessitates fancy powers like Solar Circle sorcery, Sidereal Astrology, or breeding more Exaltations.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's also not why the Exalted were created, out of setting.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted are meant to let us play werewolves, skinwalkers, and face-stealers. First Edition didn't do that right, because First Edition didn't know its own mechanics. Second Edition tried to do something else by throwing in lots of Wyld stuff and turning into anything but animals. Third Edition is going back to First Edition's simplicity, but with two editions' worth of mechanical and narrative mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Exalted were made to kill the Primordials, and each had their own distinct role in the war against them. The Sidereals couldn't do what the Solars did, the Dragon-Blooded couldn't replace the Sidereals, and the Solars could hardly take the Dragon-Blooded Host's place. What role did the Lunars have in the conflict that no other could have done? That's what I'm asking. I never said every Solar became Solar Circle Sorcerors. It's hardly relevant here anyway.<br /> <br /> As you said yourself, it doesnt look like Luna wanted her Chosen to have any kind of specific role. That's exactly my point. Why did she make them, and why did she make them that way? All we know is: Luna made her Chosen bestial because Gaia. Okay, nice. How did that help overthrowing the Primordials?<br /> I believe that's kind of an important thing to gloss over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:06:57-07:00","id":739578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=739402#post739402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exalted were made to kill the Primordials, and each had their own distinct role in the war against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each had some distinct advantages compared to the others, yes.<br /> <br /> But you still had Chosen of Battles as well as Dawn Castes. Sidereals don't JUST work the Loom, they'll also step into arenas where Solar Exalted are king. And there are few things that Sidereals can achieve with Astrology that Solars cannot eventually replicate through Solar Sorcery.<br /> <br /> The very fact of each Host having multiple Castes or Aspects makes it hard to pidgeonhole them into particular roles where one host does one thing that another host cannot do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why did she make them </div> </div> </div>Because another three to four hundred Celestial Exalted who rival the Solars for personal power before factoring in tools and infrastructural support is better than nothing? Unimaginably better.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and why did she make them that way? </div> </div> </div>What else should Luna have wanted from them? Aren't they already perfect little versions of her running around? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All we know is: Luna made her Chosen bestial because Gaia. Okay, nice. How did that help overthrowing the Primordials? </div> </div> </div>Because Beast Mode is Stronk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T16:12:45-07:00","id":739944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=739578#post739578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each had some distinct advantages compared to the others, yes.<br /> <br /> But you still had Chosen of Battles as well as Dawn Castes. Sidereals don't JUST work the Loom, they'll also step into arenas where Solar Exalted are king. And there are few things that Sidereals can achieve with Astrology that Solars cannot eventually replicate through Solar Sorcery.<br /> <br /> The very fact of each Host having multiple Castes or Aspects makes it hard to pidgeonhole them into particular roles where one host does one thing that another host cannot do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because another three to four hundred Celestial Exalted who rival the Solars for personal power before factoring in tools and infrastructural support is better than nothing? Unimaginably better.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What else should Luna have wanted from them? Aren't they already perfect little versions of her running around?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because Beast Mode is Stronk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Castes only very roughly interlap across splats. Chosen of battles aren't the guys you'll go to to lead your armies and they're no supposed to.<br /> <br /> Ok, getting more badass warriors in the fray is a good reason to create those guys.<br /> <br /> I don't think Lunars could ever be described as perfect little versions of Luna, though. Far from it.<br /> <br /> Eh.<br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T17:20:54-07:00","id":740173,"title":"","content":"The main problem I have with the Silver Pact being defined as the primary enemy of the Realm? The Realm is still there. They've been in stalemate for seven-hundred years, and now that it's all falling apart it looks like the Solars are set to deal the final blow. The Lunar Exalted? They just held out while waiting for the Shiny Bastards to get back.<br /> <br /> It just seems that the Lunars are defined as those fighting the Realm, but the Solars are set up to bring an end to that conflict. I mean, I don't know, it depends on how you run it, I guess. But I guess it's just the impression I get from Perfect Soul, the Bull of the North and whatnot.<br /> <br /> I do like the suggestion that it was the Lunar Exalted who killed the Empress though. Gives them some impact, even if that suggestion is incorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 10-29-2015, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T18:47:21-07:00","id":740506,"title":"","content":"Chosen of Battles not meant to lead armies into battle? They have War, and they have some very interesting powers in its purview. Now, they aren't meant to do the same things that Solars do by leading the enemy into battle, because they veer off from straightforward &quot;my command makes everyone better&quot;, but they're clearly still meant to lead armies into battle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=740173#post740173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main problem I have with the Silver Pact being defined as the primary enemy of the Realm? The Realm is still there. They've been in stalemate for seven-hundred years, and now that it's all falling apart it looks like the Solars are set to deal the final blow. The Lunar Exalted? They just held out while waiting for the Shiny Bastards to get back.<br /> <br /> It just seems that the Lunars are defined as those fighting the Realm, but the Solars are set up to bring an end to that conflict. I mean, I don't know, it depends on how you run it, I guess. But I guess it's just the impression I get from Perfect Soul, the Bull of the North and whatnot.<br /> <br /> I do like the suggestion that it was the Lunar Exalted who killed the Empress though. Gives them some impact, even if that suggestion is incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>They haven't been waiting. They've been faking them out, feinting and fading, all this time. You know, asymmetrical warfare, otherwise known as terrorism or fighting for freedom, depending on which side you're on and which targets are getting hit. Of course, if the state's religion already paints you as a demon and blames all the world's problems on you and a number of other assorted people (such as anyone worshiping the gods without,a Dragon-Blooded intermediary), that appellation loses a fair bit of its sting.<br /> <br /> They've been at this for that long, again, because the target has been an exceptionally hard one. The deck stacked against them had a top that couldn't be seen from the ground; now, you can probably tell where its limit is, even if it's still daunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T21:09:55-07:00","id":740785,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I know, they've been fighting the good fight for years on end, they survived and all that. It just feels to me like the entire Silver Pact is defined by a war that will probably only be won with/by the Solars.<br /> It's like, the whole fight against the Realm is -theirs- now and it's good that they've made progress over the centuries, but it's only now that the Solars are back that they have a chance. I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 10-30-2015, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T21:18:04-07:00","id":740795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=740785#post740785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know, they've been fighting the good fight for years on end, they survived and all that. It just feels to me like the entire Silver Pact is defined by a war that will probably only be won with/by the Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solars are divided and won't be able to really meet their potential for millennia, most likely five millennia, since it's specified as the length of time for which the First Age lasted. Lunars are in the trenches now and they have a whole lot fewer Wyld Hunts breathing down their neck. If Solars want anything, they'll have to fight for it, because they don't have a unified power base, and likely won't have one for quite some time. While they dither and get a start on building the most basic foundations in between having to repair them due to Realm saboteurs, the Lunars can act with relative impunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T21:19:42-07:00","id":740799,"title":"","content":"For us (the British) WW2 was a hugely pivotal moment in our culture; we rallied together as a people, we stood up to tyranny and Fascism, we endured huge amounts of bombing, we saved the Jews, we sacrificed our Empire in the cause of freedom and democracy, we learnt valuable new lessons like &quot;racism is bad&quot;, etc, etc (you might disagree with some of these, but it's how it's generally seen in Britain).<br /> Of course , if America and Russia hadn't joined the war later, we probably would had to sue for peace. We survived Hitler's bombing campaign, but we didn't have the force necessary to stop him, for that we needed others to turn up.<br /> That doesn't mean we weren't important; if we hadn't fought, Hitler would have conquered most of Europe and that would be that.<br /> <br /> This is especially relevant when we're talking about a game that's cooperative: the Lunars should have reason to try to get the Solars on side, because people want to play games with Lunars and Solars. In fact, there's probably more Solar/Lunar games than pure Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T09:08:23-07:00","id":741985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=739578#post739578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each had some distinct advantages compared to the others, yes.<br /> <br /> But you still had Chosen of Battles as well as Dawn Castes. Sidereals don't JUST work the Loom, they'll also step into arenas where Solar Exalted are king. And there are few things that Sidereals can achieve with Astrology that Solars cannot eventually replicate through Solar Sorcery.<br /> <br /> The very fact of each Host having multiple Castes or Aspects makes it hard to pidgeonhole them into particular roles where one host does one thing that another host cannot do.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the big things I love about exalted is the sheer breadth of character concepts you can embody. More than that, I love that splat is not the same thing as a character class. You can make pretty much any splat cover a massive range of character concepts. <br /> <br /> However, in 2nd Edition I always found lunars to be more defined by shapeshifting than other exalted were defined by their special powers. Sidereals are able to do amazing things with astrology and Sid martial arts, but you don't hear Sidereals described as &quot;the loom exalted&quot; nearly as much as lunars were defined by being the shapeshifting exalted. However, that's all baggage from the previous edition. we don't need that. We have new descriptions of lunars.<br /> <br /> Just as Solars are described as &quot;masters of *****&quot; (MA, Sorcery, Evocations, and creation), the lunars are &quot;Walkers in Ten Thousand Forms,&quot; &quot;Terrors in the Night,&quot; &quot;Gods of the Untamed,&quot; &quot;Armored in Silver,&quot; and... &quot;Broken Bonds...&quot;<br /> <br /> Okay, what do these mean? What <i>can</i> they mean? If we accept that these blurbs are representative of the general thrust of Lunar concepts (which seems fair) we can likely make some guesses as to the direction Lunars will be taking.<br /> <br /> <b>Walkers in Ten Thousand Forms</b><br /> <br /> Because Shapeshifting... like obviously. Still a big part of lunar concept to no one's surprise. The exact mechanics of this remain to be seen, but I remain optimistic that it'll be more useful than in 2nd Edition. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Terrors in the Night</b><br /> <br /> From the blurb:<br /> it looks like Lunars are gonna be spies, spooks, guerrillas, etc. I like the terrifying miracles from beyond the edges of the world bit. I'm interested to see if the lunars will simply be immune to the wyld as in 2E or if they'll actually be able to <i>use</i> the wyld as no other exalt can. I want to be clear: I am 100% fine with the concept of lunars being the wyld exalted so long as they're not the<i> corrupted by the wyld</i> exalted. <br /> <br /> what I'd like this to mean: <br /> Lunars are bloody hard to pin down and predict. I kinda like imagining the realm dynasts scaring their kids to bed with warnings that the lunars will get you if you don't. Especially since this is totally a thing that could happen. The lunars could be <u>everywhere</u>. It could easily be a lunar in the form of the parent sending the kid to bed so he's out of the way :-) I'd also like to see the lunars double down on the scare tactics thing. Make them really good at demorallizing an enemy. The monster in a horror movie is so much more frightening when it remains unseen. the reality is never as terrifying as the things your brain conjures up.<br /> <br /> <b>Gods of the Untamed</b><br /> <br /> From the blurb:<br /> The lunars are kinda the thousand stream river by default? Barbarian tribes worship the lunars? The name is so much cooler than the blurb i think. Ya, the communities outside realm control are likely going to be following the lunars. They're celestial exalted and you're living outside the power/protection of the realm. Still plenty of baddies ready to take out a tribe/ city/ civilization if they aren't powerful enough to resist. Lunars are gonna play into that regardless. Still, it's hard to say precisely what this blurb means for the lunars<br /> <br /> What I'd like this to mean:<br /> Lunars are able to utilize things as they are. No need to convince a tribe to give up their lifestyle to follow a lunar's way of doing things. Lunar simply points them and gives them a push. No need to reshape a landscape to grow massive crops to feed a starving city. Lunar can come in and improve the city's ability to fend for itself? Maybe improve the fertility of the area? I dunno. Even I'm not sold on everything I've said so far, but one thing I would <i>love to see</i> is rather than use wyld cauldron tech to shape the wyld into whatever you want, I'd love to see the lunar be able to use the wyld as it is to gain massive power out of it. Not for free obviously and certainly with just as much interference from the Raksha as the solars get. If the lunars live in and around the wyld all the time, maybe it's because that's where they're the strongest exalt? I don't want the lunars to become the wyld exalts exclusively, but why can't that be a character option? Same as Solars can be a master of Sorcery, or a master of evocations or a master of anything, why can't 'wyld exalt' be a valid character concept for a lunar? Not all of em, but a faction? Call them wyld seekers or wyld riders or something. <br /> <br /> <b>Armored in Silver</b><br /> <br /> Moonsilver tattoos are back. They're cool, they're visually distinct, the lunars are the only ones who can have em. Nice.<br /> <br /> Just please, don't make them <i>mandatory</i> for a playable lunar. By all means give them a hell of a benefit, but make it more than a false choice whether to have them or not. Hell, in my original post I mentioned I'd like to see un-tattood lunars able to change their caste over time (but not forced to change with the moon cycle). I'd like to see the silver pact as a political faction rather than every lunar who doesn't want to go insane and get permanently mangled by the wyld. <br /> <br /> <b>Broken Bonds</b><br /> <br /> Okay, the solar lunar bond is still a defining part of their relationship. Or at least it was before the usurpation. From the direction of things it looks like the bond is gonna be optional so that means there's design space for benefits/costs on both sides of the bond. Perhaps in the first age everybody had a bond because it was accepted that the benefits outweigh the downside for that age. Maybe right now, in this age, there is still some benefit to bonding a solar but the downsides would make most lunars pause. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the nascent bond is always there but requires something like a shape sorcery action to bring it to life. IE, there is a bond potential but mechanically no bond exists until brought into being by the actions of both solar and lunar. Above all, I cannot stress enough how much this bond should not be mandatory, nor able to be put in to place without explicit permission from both lunar and solar. <br /> <br /> So... thoughts anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:49:15-07:00","id":742395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=739253#post739253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: Ghosthead, point number 2 - Dace's account of a fight against a Realm-supported monarch in the Dawnbook of early 1e had said monarch equipped with a staff that could call storms and lightning, supplied by the Realm to help her prop up her rule. That's what they were willing to give to a mortal; imagine what they're keeping for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could extrapolate from that in that way. Not sure I'd set a great deal on an extrapolation from a section in a Caste Book opposed to the text that talks *directly* about how the Dragonblooded actually make war and what they rely on to project power, though.<br /> <br /> I get the impression from my memory of the general run of First Edition, that the Dragonblooded mostly conquer and dominate the Threshold with daiklaive, powerbow and armour in the legions, and very nice triremes in the navy and siege engines of genius beyond mortal man of contemporary manfacture, backed up with Terrestrial Circle sorcerors. While that they're certainly not pulling out the Golden Ships of Melnibone or the Ornithopers of Granbretan or anything that's a remnant of the First Age like that as an important, integral without-this-we-fall part of their strategy, so trying to deplete reserves of First Age weapons would be quite remarkably ineffective, because those are mostly lost to them and not very important to their power. Third Edition, unsurprisingly, looks like a different edition, though and whether what it does is cooler or not, we will see.<br /> <br /> Re: Sidereals as generals, they're often compared to Gandalf, and in a sense, to extend the analogy, you might not want him as the leader of armies and men if your other option is Aragorn or some ancient prince among the elf, because they're not focused on being all mysterious and spooky and wizardly while G is. But he's still going to be quite excellent in the role compared to, say, a mortal prince who is quite excellent and learned, yet has no special ties to a special magical essence of leadership and ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 10-30-2015, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T14:24:16-07:00","id":742871,"title":"","content":"Ohhh I can see that this thread is going to be testing my current attempt at a laid back attitude...<br /> <br /> Okay, something relatively neutral...<br /> <br /> The book says &quot;rage&quot;, but in the context of everything around it I see that as basically meaning &quot;Lunars have a constant itch in their soul where the Solars and the Realm used to be, and it makes them antsy&quot;. Most Lunars have responded to this by working towards tearing down what remains of the Realm and the people who usurped it; it's not even about revenge or caring about a civilization they never experienced for most of them, it's basically having memories and protective instincts for a thing that doesn't exist anymore and wanting to be <b>done</b> with it. A young Lunar fights the Realm so that they can be free of the impulse that tells them they're supposed to care about something called the Realm constantly knawing at the back of their mind while they're just trying to enjoy this new freedom to break any chains people might put around them and explore the myriad shapes.<br /> <br /> Some other Lunars have this same maddening impulse, but they use it to more directly power their personal initiatives; they occasionally seek aid from other Lunars in this, as a tit-for-tat kind of thing.<br /> <br /> The Lunars are set up as a Celestial Exalted who can be <i>apart</i> from the expected roles of the Sidereals to a greater extent and the Solars to a barely existing one*; they are that same scope of power in contrast to the others. Different Exalted are different; most Lunars would rather be able to do as they please with nobody to stop them.<br /> <br /> The return of the Solars complicates this; it seems blindingly evident to me that this complication is generally going to resolve in the direction of Lunars attempting to destroy their bonded Solars because they'd very much like to leave a past that means nothing to them behind please.<br /> <br /> I read that write-up in the Exalted chapter, and it so thoroughly beguiled me; it reminded me of this thing I read once, I can't quite remember the details, it was something like some person who is part of a society in which everybody gets bonded to a special spirit animal which they have a certain mystical emotional connection to, and she's a bit of a rebel, but at some point she encounters her animal and she feels the bond forming and it's so right and it makes so much feel clear and safe in her soul, and she reaches out to the innocent thing that trusts her entirely and she breaks its neck.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I got an impression from the antagonists section that totems may not even be a thing at all.<br /> <br /> * the idea that Exalted in general are hardwired to social roles is pretty terrible, but never mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T15:10:07-07:00","id":742999,"title":"","content":"You're thinking of Mrs. Coulter in <i>His Dark Materials, </i>Isator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T15:15:04-07:00","id":743007,"title":"","content":"Okay, sure, the lunars don't have a specific role in the way dragon-bloods, sidereals or solars have. That's kind of the point, don't you think? Not undefined, <i>flexible</i>.<br /> <br /> Imagine a major wyld incursion. Astrology is bonkered and if you step inside to do battle you find out you can't use any of the normal abilities. You must use afgnurk, z'kran or vindelfide. <i>What do you mean </i>'you don't have dots in any of those abilities or charms for them'? Are you just gonna stand there like a gnarkel-fronk?<br /> This is where you send in lunars so they can kick those za--traff's in the krunkel-huesen!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1226-gammelbraxen","name":"Gammelbraxen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T15:27:15-07:00","id":743034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gammelbraxen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743007#post743007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, sure, the lunars don't have a specific role in the way dragon-bloods, sidereals or solars have. That's kind of the point, don't you think? Not undefined, <i>flexible</i>.<br /> <br /> Imagine a major wyld incursion. Astrology is bonkered and if you step inside to do battle you find out you can't use any of the normal abilities. You must use afgnurk, z'kran or vindelfide. <i>What do you mean </i>'you don't have dots in any of those abilities or charms for them'? Are you just gonna stand there like a gnarkel-fronk?<br /> This is where you send in lunars so they can kick those za--traff's in the krunkel-huesen!</div> </div> </div> </div>You just defined their role as troubleshooting things that other exalts cannot effectively face... That's fine, but you can't say that's not a specific role.<br /> <br /> Saying the lunars have no specific role in in the exalted host is tantamount to saying that they were almost superfluous to to the host. <br /> <br /> &quot;The solars are the generals and the greatest warriors of the host, the most powerful to lead from the front! The Sidereals are their council and master of intrigue and teaching and stuff. They bend the very stars to our cause! The Dragon Blooded are the backbone of our forces! They are the footsoliders and most important resource! The lunars are.. over there. They seem to be doing... stuff... the stuff no one else wants to do... EXALTS! FORWARD!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T15:32:30-07:00","id":743046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Britain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're thinking of Mrs. Coulter in His Dark Materials, Isator.</div> </div> </div> </div> How do you figure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T16:15:27-07:00","id":743186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743034#post743034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying the lunars have no specific role in in the exalted host is tantamount to saying that they were almost superfluous to to the host.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, this might be a language thing (english isn't my native language). What I meant was that lunars didn't have a <i>set </i>role in the way the other exalts had (soldiers, generals, advisors and so on). Adapting to the unexpected is certainly a role as such, but training and planning for it is pretty hard when you don't know what to expect. So flexibility, adapting to a situation, like Luna changing face and manners to best meet an uncertain situation. Until they have a solution and use it (or go to any of the other exalts if they are better suited for the solution I guess).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1226-gammelbraxen","user":"Gammelbraxen","date":". 10-30-2015, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1226-gammelbraxen","name":"Gammelbraxen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T16:42:17-07:00","id":743223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know, they've been fighting the good fight for years on end, they survived and all that. It just feels to me like the entire Silver Pact is defined by a war that will probably only be won with/by the Solars. It's like, the whole fight against the Realm is -theirs- now and it's good that they've made progress over the centuries, but it's only now that the Solars are back that they have a chance. I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're assuming that the Lunars being close to finally, utterly destroying the Realm isn't the kind of thing that the Solars need to save the world from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:54:17-07:00","id":743351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=742395#post742395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could extrapolate from that in that way. Not sure I'd set a great deal on an extrapolation from a section in a Caste Book opposed to the text that talks *directly* about how the Dragonblooded actually make war and what they rely on to project power, though.<br /> <br /> I get the impression from my memory of the general run of First Edition, that the Dragonblooded mostly conquer and dominate the Threshold with daiklaive, powerbow and armour in the legions, and very nice triremes in the navy and siege engines of genius beyond mortal man of contemporary manfacture, backed up with Terrestrial Circle sorcerors. While that they're certainly not pulling out the Golden Ships of Melnibone or the Ornithopers of Granbretan or anything that's a remnant of the First Age like that as an important, integral without-this-we-fall part of their strategy, so trying to deplete reserves of First Age weapons would be quite remarkably ineffective, because those are mostly lost to them and not very important to their power. Third Edition, unsurprisingly, looks like a different edition, though and whether what it does is cooler or not, we will see.</div> </div> </div> </div>The challenge is to get them to feel that the situation has escalated to that point. Social engineering and other aspects of their particular type of warfare come into play here, getting false reports in and then using other means to get the First Age hulls into trouble serious enough for them to suffer damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Re: Sidereals as generals, they're often compared to Gandalf, and in a sense, to extend the analogy, you might not want him as the leader of armies and men if your other option is Aragorn or some ancient prince among the elf, because they're not focused on being all mysterious and spooky and wizardly while G is. But he's still going to be quite excellent in the role compared to, say, a mortal prince who is quite excellent and learned, yet has no special ties to a special magical essence of leadership and ruling. </div> </div> </div>The comparison to Gandalf isn't very apt, I think, given that Gandalf never actually led anything instead of acting as counselor, and Sidereals have Charms and Resplendency effects that are a great deal more direct than this (The Captain, for example, tends to require you to actually be in charge and leading, not just an advisor). The only reason that they use light touches is because they're overworked; getting more fully involved takes more time out of their schedules, and no one wants to skip on the Celestial blow parties in heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:58:40-07:00","id":743356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743034#post743034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just defined their role as troubleshooting things that other exalts cannot effectively face... That's fine, but you can't say that's not a specific role.<br /> <br /> Saying the lunars have no specific role in in the exalted host is tantamount to saying that they were almost superfluous to to the host.<br /> <br /> &quot;The solars are the generals and the greatest warriors of the host, the most powerful to lead from the front! The Sidereals are their council and master of intrigue and teaching and stuff. They bend the very stars to our cause! The Dragon Blooded are the backbone of our forces! They are the footsoliders and most important resource! The lunars are.. over there. They seem to be doing... stuff... the stuff no one else wants to do... EXALTS! FORWARD!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They were meant to be werewolves. <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?670878-Exalted-Where-we-speculate-about-Lunar-Exalted-in-Exalted-3rd-edition&amp;p=16307821#post16307821\" target=\"_blank\">Real truth, more or less</a>. This means that they don't fit neatly into a standard military organizational structure, but that can definitely engage in tasks that will benefit them. The present Lunars are even further from that purpose, of course, drifting off since the Realm started, but in the end, they're shapeshifting heroes with a monstrous streak. Remember, the entirety of their Charms involve statements of &quot;I am&quot; rather than &quot;I do&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T18:21:05-07:00","id":743405,"title":"","content":"I think one should note how the new core opts to describe Solars as figures who <i>rose</i> to the highest or most significant positions in the armies of the gods and the Realm; they were neither made for nor appointed to it. Even considering the more ingrained role of the Sidereal and Terrestrial Exalted, I would say that any kind of straightforward hierarchy or strategic structure was not hashed out initially (certainly, I can imagine that a clan of several hundred related Exalted was not initially all over the idea of taking orders from Celestials, and possessed the heft to back that up). Considering John's old points about how the Lunars were different things between the Primordial War and the First Age, I can even readily imagine that the whole Bond thing took some time to build up, and that prior to that they had a fairly straightforward deal of &quot;individualistic unstoppable, beautiful god-monster&quot;; I can even imagine that, prior to finding their place alongside the Solars, Lunars didn't have any kind of Caste at all (then they developed five that could adapt to roles in the Realm and bonding to a Solar, and then forcefully remade them to fit a hostile world in which Realm and Solars were kaput).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:23:51-07:00","id":743644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=742871#post742871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's not even about revenge or caring about a civilization they never experienced for most of them, it's basically having memories and protective instincts for a thing that doesn't exist anymore and wanting to be <b>done</b> with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may not be such a driving factor for newer Lunars as &quot;I want to kill these bastards who are trying to kill me before they succeed&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I read that write-up in the Exalted chapter, and it so thoroughly beguiled me; it reminded me of this thing I read once, I can't quite remember the details, it was something like some person who is part of a society in which everybody gets bonded to a special spirit animal which they have a certain mystical emotional connection to, and she's a bit of a rebel, but at some point she encounters her animal and she feels the bond forming and it's so right and it makes so much feel clear and safe in her soul, and she reaches out to the innocent thing that trusts her entirely and she breaks its neck. </div> </div> </div>Yikes. I want no part of <i>that.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, I got an impression from the antagonists section that totems may not even be a thing at all. </div> </div> </div>Do tell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:36:08-07:00","id":743664,"title":"","content":"I assume because there were no rules for totems whatsoever? That it just had &quot;these are the animals you can turn into?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a possibility, but I\u200b assumed it was just that you don't get any special benefit turning into one. I mean, presumably you still start with an animal form.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:40:02-07:00","id":743670,"title":"","content":"Letting players choose whichever totem they want without mechanical concerns seems fulfilled by giving no special benefit to the spirit shape.<br /> <br /> So I could choose a dog Totem just because I like dogs, and not because I feel pressured to have a bird true shape or a tyrant lizard true shape. I can have those as well, and none of them are any cheaper than the others.<br /> <br /> Also, form lock died in a fire. So.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:49:40-07:00","id":743691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743670#post743670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, form lock died in a fire. So.</div> </div> </div> </div>Halle-fuc*ing-lujah.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T21:04:36-07:00","id":743739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743670#post743670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Letting players choose whichever totem they want without mechanical concerns seems fulfilled by giving no special benefit to the spirit shape.<br /> <br /> So I could choose a dog Totem just because I like dogs, and not because I feel pressured to have a bird true shape or a tyrant lizard true shape. I can have those as well, and none of them are any cheaper than the others.<br /> <br /> Also, form lock died in a fire. So.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Totem could just have fluff effects. Like, when you use Armour-Forming Technique (or 3rd ed equivalent), the dog totem gets thick fur and the Tyrant Lizard gets scales, but they still get the same soak bonus. And your Tell of course.<br /> Also, presumably your caste/favoured \u200battributes should reflect your Totem (or rather, your Totem reflects your Caste/Favoured attributes) but that doesn't need any rules.<br /> <br /> Another possibility; a long time ago, Hatewheel said he was considering letting your Totem letting you buy appropriate charms easier. For example, you're a Dog totem Lunar, so you can somehow buy Smell-based charms easier. There wasn't much explanation as to how this would work though (I guess it was an idea, not something fully formed). Could be what they get instead of Supernal (which does not imply it works in any way similar).<br /> That does mean that there is still reason to choose certain Totems for certain charms, but that's like it's worth playing a swordsman to get Melee charms: they'd probably be charms you wanted for your concept anyway. If a Tyrant Lizard, a Bat and a Cat all let you buy 5 or 6 charms more easily, one isn't really stronger than another.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T21:08:48-07:00","id":743747,"title":"","content":"Another 2 thoughts (that are related) on Totems.<br /> <br /> Firstly, Chimeras. These \u200bapparently will exist, and be Lunars who've mixed together multiple totems. This implies Totems do something mechanically.<br /> <br /> Secondly, God-Beasts. If Lunars are the heroic monsters of the world... should they be able to create their own mythic totem form? Maybe by mixing totem forms (eagle+lion=Chimeras) or by having charms that enhance forms (like Gift charms, but you can use them for your totem form? So your cat Totem Lunar can turn into a mighty Cat monster with excellent stats? Is that perhaps better as enhancements to animal forms, or as a monstrous form with specific stats? Or perhaps this doesn't need anything to do with Totems: maybe Lunars should just have a lot of buff charms you can use whenever you take animal form, regardless of your Totem, otherwise it encourages combat totems again).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T21:41:41-07:00","id":743833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743747#post743747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lunars are the heroic monsters of the world... should they be able to create their own mythic totem form?</div> </div> </div> </div>The form is mythic because the Lunar is a Lunar.<br /> <br /> Even the simplest lion spirit shape becomes the Nemean Lion when the Full Moon invests in Stamina Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T22:08:19-07:00","id":743855,"title":"","content":"So the Lunar's charms do often revolve around buffing his animal forms (Totem form? Or any animal form).<br /> But do they buff his animal form better than they buff his human form (as they previously buffed DBT better, or at least quicker)?<br /> <br /> Certainly I feel that upon transforming into a Lion, the Lunar should be able to active charms that buff said form for the duration of that form (to represent turning into the Nemean Lion, rather than a regular Lion), as opposed to taking a simple action to get a scene-long buff like a Solar would.<br /> <br /> Or... do the Stamina charms permanently buff his Lion form?<br /> <br /> Or... is this represented by him using better dice pools because he has better stats? If so, what do the charms do?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T22:45:15-07:00","id":743882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743664#post743664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume because there were no rules for totems whatsoever? That it just had &quot;these are the animals you can turn into?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a possibility, but I\u200b assumed it was just that you don't get any special benefit turning into one. I mean, presumably you still start with an animal form.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunar descriptions don't include details on the totem mostly because that is not an efficient use of wordcount. The first animal called out in each template's list of forms is what I notionally designated as their spirit shape. <br /> <br /> It also holds absolutely zero bearing as to what future Lunar mechanics will look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T23:17:07-07:00","id":743894,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's the impression I got.<br /> <br /> Holden said elsewhere that those Lunar charms are really just placeholders and you shouldn't think too much about them (same presumably with Sidereal, Liminal, etc charms) because the book hasn't been written yet.<br /> <br /> I assume that the general theme of them is not far out from what the devs are currently thinking about Lunars: they're not going to suddenly become Alex Mercer protean blobs in the book, it's just that we shouldn't expect the rules to stay the same.<br /> <br /> I also wondered about dice pools: in there, Lunars use the animal's physical dice pools, not the animal's physical attributes. On the other hand, since all the animals in the Core don't have attributes, and were apparently specifically written with Lunars in mind, that makes me think it will stay this way (with maybe charms letting you use the better of your dice pool or the animal's).<br /> <br /> I hope they keep a similar Tell mechanic though, I like that.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T23:19:03-07:00","id":743897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743855#post743855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Lunar's charms do often revolve around buffing his animal forms (Totem form? Or any animal form).<br /> But do they buff his animal form better than they buff his human form (as they previously buffed DBT better, or at least quicker)?<br /> <br /> Certainly I feel that upon transforming into a Lion, the Lunar should be able to active charms that buff said form for the duration of that form (to represent turning into the Nemean Lion, rather than a regular Lion), as opposed to taking a simple action to get a scene-long buff like a Solar would.<br /> <br /> Or... do the Stamina charms permanently buff his Lion form?<br /> <br /> Or... is this represented by him using better dice pools because he has better stats? If so, what do the charms do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar BuysStamina charms.<br /> <br /> Lunar becomes super tough.<br /> <br /> Lunar turns into lion.<br /> <br /> The charms that made the lunar super tough are still there.<br /> <br /> Thus, Lunar is still Super Tough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T23:57:33-07:00","id":743914,"title":"","content":"Given that animals don't seem to have any attribute stats, I assume the Lunar's are used and any boost to the base stamina applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T23:59:58-07:00","id":743917,"title":"","content":"As it was in 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> But... that's just the way that Solar charms work. And I feel it doesn't really make you think &quot;Wow, my Lunar turned into an awesome super-lion!&quot; in the same way.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be very bothered by Lunars activating scene-long charms, but what I really want is some sort of connection whereby you activate charms at the same time you transform (rather than transforming, then spending a Simple action to activate Claws of the Silver Moon) so it feels like you turned into a badass monster-form, rather than you turned into an animal, then activated some other charm.<br /> Like Gift+DBT in 2nd ed. When you turned into a giant lizard-men with incredibly thick scales and huge silver claws who constantly regenerated, that did feel like you'd turned into a badass monster, rather than turned into a hybrid and then activated charms to buff. Also, your giant soak didn't disappear after a scene; why should it, you're still a huge badass monster, it's not like you turned back.<br /> Not saying it has to work like that, but I want that feeling and thematic.<br /> Do you see what I mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-31-2015, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T00:06:05-07:00","id":743926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743917#post743917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... that's just the way that Solar charms work. And I feel it doesn't really make you think &quot;Wow, my Lunar turned into an awesome super-lion!&quot; in the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 3e paradigm seems to be that you feel like you turned into an awesome super-lion because animals are<i> goddamn hardcore</i>, not because you get a bunch of charms to turn a weaksauce lion form into something that's actually useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T00:15:37-07:00","id":743929,"title":"","content":"Okay... so what do Lunar charms do? I mean, yes, a Lion has better stats than before, and merits. But if we're saying that (beyond presumably extending what forms the Lunar can take) the charms don't buff your animal forms, do they interact with the idea of turning into the Nemean lion at all? Or are they about entirely separate things?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T00:25:36-07:00","id":743936,"title":"","content":"I should also say: turning into a Lion and being awesome at combat because Lions are actually good at combat is definitely great at Essence 1. No more will PCs only fight in human or DBT (or occasionally Tyrant Lizard) form. <br /> But when you're Essence 4\u200b, a Lion's stats and special attacks are not going to be awesome at combat because the things you're up against are much better than before. So charms that buff stats and provide more special attacks seem pretty appropriate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T00:30:52-07:00","id":743940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743917#post743917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... that's just the way that Solar charms work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a bad thing? If Solars have charms that let them perform feats of strength, Lunars can't have those charms or charms that work similarly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I feel it doesn't really make you think &quot;Wow, my Lunar turned into an awesome super-lion!&quot; in the same way. </div> </div> </div>Suddenly having camouflage in the wilderness, night vision, being able to move silently without penalty, an ambush attack, and a maul attack should make you feel like a lion. You\u2019re getting a suite of great cat abilities.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a lion that can leap over a twenty foot wall, swim through lava, or roar loud enough to crack stones\u2026 yes, you\u2019ll need a separate charm for those abilities. Or maybe drink the blood of a super lion if you can find one.<br /> <br /> Lion = Basic shapechanging<br /> Superlion = Shapechanging and some charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743917#post743917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be very bothered by Lunars activating scene-long charms, but what I really want is some sort of connection whereby you activate charms at the same time you transform (rather than transforming, then spending a Simple action to activate Claws of the Silver Moon) so it feels like you turned into a badass monster-form, rather than you turned into an animal, then activated some other charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you want a shantai type animalistic form that you put XP into. We might be getting something like that.<br /> <br /> However, lots of players would like be able to use that stone shattering cry when they're a lion, falcon, or oxen. Not simply when they're a lion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T00:54:32-07:00","id":743952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743940#post743940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lion = Basic shapechanging<br /> Superlion = Shapechanging and some charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's what I'm getting at. As I said, turning into a Lion is fine at Essence 1, because it's a badass fighter/ambusher, but without charms to improve it, it's not going to work so well at high level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you want a shantai type animalistic form that you put XP into. We might be getting something like that. </div> </div> </div>I think I would be fine with that as one thing Lunars can do. Though I don't know what you mean by Shantai? \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, lots of players would like be able to use that stone shattering cry when they're a lion, falcon, or oxen. Not simply when they're a lion. </div> </div> </div>That's not what I'm getting at. I'm not saying &quot;buy a charm that buffs one animal form&quot;. I'm saying charms should buff any form when you turn into it. So you buy, say, Mountainous Spirit Meditation, and you can turn into a giant Lion, a giant Falcon, or a giant Oxen (or regular ones). Or you buy Claws of the Silver Moon and you can turn into a Lion with deadly silver claws, or a falcon with deadly silver claws, or an oxen with silver... hooves, I guess? Or you buy Hide-Toughening Essence and turn into the Nemean Lion whose hide no sword can cut, or the Bull with Iron Skin, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Whereas in 2e you turn into a lion. You can use Mountainous Spirit Expression if it's your totem, otherwise not. Then you spend another action growing your deadly silver talons which turn off at the end of the scene. Also, you can use Hide-Toughening Essence reflexively (though you'll probably wait until someone hits you), which again turns off at the end of the scene (though this is less the issue than the simple action to grow your talons). This doesn't really make it feel like you've turned into a super-lion or super-ox or super-falcon, it feels more like you've turned into a lion and then throw stuff on top of it as necessary. I'm saying they should work more like Gift charms* to make it feel like part of the transformation.<br /> <br /> This isn't really a big change, though it leads into some thematic significance. But then, its thematic significance than I think the devs would like to go into: I think they'd like to see Lunars changing into animals for a lot more than sneaking, flying and disguise (since if you want combat, you turn into DBT).<br /> <br /> *I mean, maybe the mechanics will change entirely and this won't make sense, that's fine. But I hope you can see what I'm getting at in terms of how the mechanics express themes?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T02:36:16-07:00","id":744053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may not be such a driving factor for newer Lunars as &quot;I want to kill these bastards who are trying to kill me before they succeed&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but we've known about that for ages, and it's fairly obvious, and it's not necessarily distinct to the Lunars. I'm trying to drive at what I saw as a distinct quality of their mystical condition, and a basis for their extreme emotional state, and a thing that can motivate them to take part in the conflict even if they were never personally affected by it (one way or another, there are going to be Lunars who were beyond the reach of any Wyld Hunt, and I don't want them to be a closed case) or have the means to kind of evade it forever.<br /> <br /> That and I would think it was the kind of thing that would appeal to everybody who was ever put off by the stated new direction on the grounds that they would think many modern Lunars wouldn't care about the Old Realm; an implication of &quot;hey, many of them don't actually want to be, and they're taking part in the whole deal so that they don't have to be and can actually move forward&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I want no part of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, keep in mind that in this case the &quot;innocent mystical spirit animal&quot; is a friggin' Solar. I don't see what would be so controversial about &quot;many Lunars would see the restoration of the Bond as a step backwards, and will enforce this with violence if necessary&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunar descriptions don't include details on the totem mostly because that is not an efficient use of wordcount. The first animal called out in each template's list of forms is what I notionally designated as their spirit shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense; I'm good either way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">so what do Lunar charms do?</div> </div> </div> </div>You kind of seem to be arguing against yourself here...<br /> <br /> Hmm, I could have sworn I saw something that suggested that Exalted who could turn into animals could have means to automatically use latent and even some magical capabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T02:53:35-07:00","id":744073,"title":"","content":"It's more that I'm trying to explore where this is going to go. Obviously, Lunar charms were rather ill-defined thematically in 2nd ed; some were transformation, some attribute-based (you're so strong they can't parry! You're so clever you remember things easily), some illusions, some Silver Solar.<br /> <br /> On magical and latent abilities, I think one of the writers said they could get them with charms maybe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T03:57:39-07:00","id":744182,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, I feel as though these new Charms introducing the premise of things with application or reset conditions according to ways that you act... I would say that you could give a Lunar numerous Charms that were rather similar (but not identical, because we don't want to be reading the same Charms over and over) to those of a Solar, and still make them feel significantly different by only giving them their free full Excellency when they act the part of a terrifying god-monster, or make their reset conditions based on being terrifying or making maiming attacks or what have you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T04:59:38-07:00","id":744255,"title":"","content":"That is true, if a little dull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T05:10:46-07:00","id":744261,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying an entire Charm set like that, just if there was a certain line of Charms that were based on enhancing actions, but the actions all followed a certain image and were centered around something that rewarded acting with the personality or approach of a Lunar, I think that's an avenue to make somebody feel like a Lunar without needing to make all of their Charms involve a heavy transformation or animal invocation bit, even if those are the meat to the potatoes that I'm describing. None of this is a direct response to your desire for Charms that are like Gift effects for one or more animal shapes in general, just my part of the discussion of where Lunars might go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T05:33:06-07:00","id":744272,"title":"","content":"It doesn't have to be a response: I feel what I said was a minor point that perhaps got over-inflated in discussion.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I see your point about meat and potatoes: to a certain extent, Lunars probably have to have some charms that are similar to Solars, just because they're basic charm effects. Like, say, penalty negators as defence charms. Or the example charm that reduces Decisive damage by 3. But those are not really the sort of charms that are only useable once.<br /> Useable once charms tend to be something special, or some form of super-excellency.<br /> Also super-excellencies on Attribute exalts (I mean things like &quot;once per day you get a full free excellency&quot; or &quot;once per day, you can apply double 8s to an X roll&quot;) might be weird to balance... or maybe it doesn't matter if they're more applicable when you can still only use them once per day (and a free full Dex excellency isn't so much of a saving).<br /> So, I think maybe it's a good thematic idea, but I'm not sure it'd work very well that way (of reset conditions). The things that are reset that way are likely already different enough (except the super-excellencies). Not to say those couldn't be reset that way, just that it doesn't help so much with basic charms.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I noticed a few of the example Lunar charms had some benefits against people who were scared of the Lunar. I wonder if they will have a fair few charms that are powered by being the monster that haunts people's nightmares. I think that works well as a minor theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-31-2015, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T05:47:35-07:00","id":744292,"title":"","content":"When I say &quot;reset conditions&quot;, I'm not talking about the Charm, I'm talking about what you need to do in order to be able to use the Charm again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T05:56:50-07:00","id":744309,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's what I thought.<br /> My point is that the kind of charms that can only be used once, and thus need a reset condition, tend not be basic meat-and-potatoes stuff, but your fancy once-per-combat (or once-per-day) stuff, which is easier to make more individual and thematic by itself than something like, say, a charm that lets you ignore penalties to your Defence, or increase your Guile. The exception being the charms that say something like &quot;you can use a free excellency once per day&quot;, which I agree could benefit from this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T08:14:42-07:00","id":744500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=743936#post743936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should also say: turning into a Lion and being awesome at combat because Lions are actually good at combat is definitely great at Essence 1. No more will PCs only fight in human or DBT (or occasionally Tyrant Lizard) form.<br /> But when you're Essence 4\u200b, a Lion's stats and special attacks are not going to be awesome at combat because the things you're up against are much better than before. So charms that buff stats and provide more special attacks seem pretty appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah And Lunars will have those regardless of what form they're in<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Lunar could spend some XP to unlock the latent and supernatural abilities that a Lion might have if trained by an Exalt, thus making it so that you turn into a better lion.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the lion shape is your totem in which case we've been given implications that the Lunar can evolve the Totem.'<br /> <br /> Or maybe the lion is still you totem, but you're a chimera, so it's a twice-as-big, flying lion with crocodile scales, eagle talons coming out of the knuckles above the regular claws, a scorpion tail, and the tail, claws, talons, and fangs all have that flesh eating venom from that one wyld mutant you ate last month.<br /> <br /> Or you do some combination of the above.<br /> <br /> In any case, charms that only apply when you turn into an animal are not needed to make the animal/totem form better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T08:23:29-07:00","id":744508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=744500#post744500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah And Lunars will have those regardless of what form they're in<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Lunar could spend some XP to unlock the latent and supernatural abilities that a Lion might have if trained by an Exalt, thus making it so that you turn into a better lion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine so, (though I think probably you should be able to cross-apply them: if you buy one bird-of-prey's ambush strike, you should probably get it for all birds-of-prey that can learn it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or maybe the lion shape is your totem in which case we've been given implications that the Lunar can evolve the Totem.' </div> </div> </div>Have we? That sounds good, though this gets back to the issue Sunder-the-Gold points out, of how to do that without making some Totems clearly superior to others so you get 3 Tyrant Lizard-totem Lunars for each Cat-totem Lunar. I'm sure there's ways to do it well though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or maybe the lion is still you totem, but you're a chimera, so it's a twice-as-big, flying lion with crocodile scales, eagle talons coming out of the knuckles above the regular claws, a scorpion tail, and the tail, claws, talons, and fangs all have that flesh eating venom from that one wyld mutant you ate last month. </div> </div> </div>That is exactly what I'd like my Lunar to be able to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In any case, charms that only apply when you turn into an animal are not needed to make the animal/totem form better. </div> </div> </div>I never said they should. There's no need for charms that only apply in animal form, except maybe stuff like increasing (or reducing the size).<br /> All I said was that the act of transformation should allow you to use charms to buff yourself, rather than taking a Simple action 5 seconds later, so that they feel like part of the transformation (and also they should last for while you're in that form). So that Claws of the Silver Moon represents you turning into a silver-clawed lion rather than you turning into a Lion.<br /> This is a)pretty small (but people seemed to turn it into a big thing: but then, I do think it's a big thing thematically) and b)was already done with Gift charms, so is clearly easily doable.<br /> I mean, when my Lunar goes DBT, he turns into a stone-skinned, silver-clawed, regenerating monster. When he turns into a Bear, he just turns into a Bear. Maybe said Bear is also covered with thick armour plates for one fight, but it feels like he's Bear+Armour-Forming Technique rather than a super-tough Bear (and looks like it). And the bear doesn't have silver claws, because I'm fighting for my life, I don't have time to activate a scene-long buff, there's dudes trying to stab me and I don't have any Ox-Bodies, I need to take them down fast not sit around growing claws.<br /> So, basically, if I'm in a serious combat, the only creature I'll turn into is DBT (or a bird, and flee), which means my awesome cool ability to turn into a bear is primarily used for scaring people in a way that doesn't make them call the Wyld Hunt (I admit turning into a Tyrant Lizard is pretty tempting, though it's generally too big to be practical, but that does mean again that several of my charms won't be used so much), rather than ripping people's faces off.<br /> <br /> This isn't really a very big point, but people seem to have run with what I said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-31-2015, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T09:15:47-07:00","id":744581,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've used terminology without considering what it means to others... when I said &quot;meat and potatoes&quot; what I meant was... Lunars are probably going to have Charms that, whatever their actual mechanics, just plain would not look like supernatural powers to an external observer. Say... a bunch of Dexterity Charms that could be used to enhance sword fighting in a manner and with precepts distinct from Solar Melee Charms, and to a person looking would &quot;just&quot; seem like an unusually fkexible sword fighter. Those are the potatoes. The stuff that is very apparently, overtly the expression of the furious, bestial might of a Lunar, whether it be shifting to a war form or ripping a bear in half accompanied by the spectral image of a rending animal, that is the meat. What I am suggesting is that you can have the potatoes, and actually make them significant, even iconic Lunar Charms, the kinds of Charms you could build a character around, and dodge a lot of the Silver Solar problems by surrounding such Charms in incentives and conditions that make the character feel like a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T09:23:39-07:00","id":744598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=744053#post744053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, keep in mind that in this case the &amp;quot;innocent mystical spirit animal&amp;quot; is a friggin' Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it doesn't seem that way in your example, so what was that psychopath's excuse?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> means to automatically use latent and even some magical capabilities. </div> </div> </div>Anything you need to train a pet to use, a Lunar needs to spend XP to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T09:30:54-07:00","id":744607,"title":"","content":"The way I'd like to see it is &quot;Low level charms are using your essence to enhance your attributes, mid level charms are essence+Shape-shifting to enhance your atributes, and high level charms are blatantly supernatural-there's no way you aren't a Lunar.&quot;<br /> <br /> Using strength as an example, the low level charms would just be using your essenc to increase your raw strength to carry more or hit harder, possibly at the same time(As opposed to the Solar equivelent which would be spending essence to make you better at carrying or hitting, but not both)<br /> <br /> Mid level strength charms would be things like bulking up to make yourself even stronger or adjusting your musculature to be more efficient or growing fangs and claws to make you even better at hand to hand combat(Or making the natural weapons of your animal form better.)<br /> <br /> And then the High Level charms are things like becoming a glorious godly giant(or giant godbeast), a living wall of rippling muscles with bulging veins, armed with fangs and claws of silver forged when you channeled the raw, wild power of Luna and the essence of your own soul to reshape your limps into the perfect tools for killing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T12:13:24-07:00","id":744821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">so what was that psychopath's excuse?</div> </div> </div> </div> About the same as a Lunar who might want nothing more to do with the Bond. Also, it's an animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T19:32:02-07:00","id":745588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=744581#post744581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I've used terminology without considering what it means to others... when I said &quot;meat and potatoes&quot; what I meant was... Lunars are probably going to have Charms that, whatever their actual mechanics, just plain would not look like supernatural powers to an external observer. Say... a bunch of Dexterity Charms that could be used to enhance sword fighting in a manner and with precepts distinct from Solar Melee Charms, and to a person looking would &quot;just&quot; seem like an unusually fkexible sword fighter. Those are the potatoes. The stuff that is very apparently, overtly the expression of the furious, bestial might of a Lunar, whether it be shifting to a war form or ripping a bear in half accompanied by the spectral image of a rending animal, that is the meat. What I am suggesting is that you can have the potatoes, and actually make them significant, even iconic Lunar Charms, the kinds of Charms you could build a character around, and dodge a lot of the Silver Solar problems by surrounding such Charms in incentives and conditions that make the character feel like a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would work fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T20:05:46-07:00","id":745634,"title":"","content":"By the by, has anybody talked about Ma-Ha-Suchi yet? I've had this idea for a while of some powerful Lunar in the East who basically wants nothing more than to be left to his house in peace and has little interest in the Silver Pact (and kept thinking that that goatfolk horde being prepared to go on a rampage towards the sea was the height of lunacy), so I'm rather tickled by how such a figure is not only written into the core, but Ma-Ha-Suchi was turned into it. Although, my idea was for a character who was more or less detached from the world but for the occasional Wyld Hunt or misguided Pact recruiter, so it's interesting to see how and why this version keeps having the world intrude upon him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T20:21:10-07:00","id":745657,"title":"","content":"I would have thought Raksi is the one who wants to be left alone so she can pursue her arcane studies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T20:32:34-07:00","id":745665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=744821#post744821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> About the same as a Lunar who might want nothing more to do with the Bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because I'm totally sold on that animal being the same as a Solar who could at least potentially be a raging dickhead with a hypnotic tongue and no value for the lives and dignity of others.<br /> <br /> A Lunar would already be enough of a dick for wanting to murder a Solar Mate who just now learned of her existence, before she knows the first thing about him... but THAT girl you describe is outright criminally insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T20:46:53-07:00","id":745676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, because I'm totally sold on that animal being the same as a Solar who could at least potentially be a raging dickhead with a hypnotic tongue and no value for the lives and dignity of others.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm reminded of a recent critical analysis of a bit of children's literature I read recently, in which somebody deconstructed the idea of somebody being okay with the possibility of belonging to a <u>nice</u> master. I'm sure the relationship with Solars in the First Age had a lot more going on with it than being an owner, but I still don't think it's much of a stretch to think that there are Lunars who don't want to be bonded with Solars of any characteristics. As for responding to that with murder: cultural values differ in different times and places. I think that even by todays standards, murdering somebody so that they don't fill a mystical gap in your soul with a sense of dedication and belonging would come across as more reasonable than, say, a Norseman who would murder a friend in response to the slight of being given a gift that was too valuable. I mean, there's a reason so many societies have treated murder as something you pay a fine for. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">THAT girl you describe is outright criminally insane</div> </div> </div> </div> It's an <i>animal</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T21:31:53-07:00","id":745717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=745676#post745676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an <i>animal</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a <i>dependent</i>, by the sound of things. Not a would-be master.<br /> <br /> So, this line of arguing is probably off-topic. If the murdered creature was a familiar rather than a Solar, it's not analogous in a way that I need to attack or that you need to defend","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T22:41:12-07:00","id":745837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=745676#post745676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an <i>animal</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're thinking of Mrs. Coulter in <i>His Dark Materials, </i>Isator. </div> </div> </div>&quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A </span></span></span><b>d\u00e6mon</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA_for_English\" target=\"_blank\">/\u02c8di\u02d0m\u0259n/</a></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> is a type of fictional being in the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_Pullman\" target=\"_blank\">Philip Pullman</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> fantasy trilogy </span></span></span><i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/His_Dark_Materials\" target=\"_blank\">His Dark Materials</a></i><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. D\u00e6mons are the <b>external physical manifestation of a person's 'inner-self'</b> that takes the form of an animal. D\u00e6mons have <b>human intelligence</b>, are capable of h<b>uman speech</b>\u2014regardless of the form they take\u2014and<b> usually behave as though they are independent of their humans</b></span></span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> If it's as smart as a human, it's human for the intents and purposes of morality and ethics.<br /> <br /> You described a woman who essentially murdered the sentient, sapient, intelligent enough to communicate with her, literal embodiment of her soul... Because she didn't want to commit. To a being who was, essentially, herself.<br /> <br /> That's pretty fucking insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 11-01-2015, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T23:05:09-07:00","id":745902,"title":"","content":"Even if it weren't part of her soul or it didn't have human intelligence, we're talking about a woman who responds to feeling an emotional bond with an animal by killing it. That's not what I would call healthy.<br /> <br /> That said, some of the Lunar write-up suggests they feel an urge to 'break chains.' I expect their Essence Fever also pushes them to wildness. The intermingling of some past memories of how Solars sometimes act and the sudden, possibly supernatural bond with another might freak a Lunar out.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind if a Lunar and Solar greeted one another with a <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Y1g-B8BJzwc\" target=\"_blank\">superhero style</a> slug out before becoming best buds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T23:58:02-07:00","id":745989,"title":"","content":"When Babar the Munificent, defrocked tattooed Immaculate Monk, wanted bandit, and sleazy sex-cult leader, met Dupree, the greatest craftsman in Great Forks, and I said &quot;Dupree's your Solar Mate, get your auto-intimacy to him&quot;, Babar was... not happy. He mainly ignored Dupree, while bitching to the others about how terrible Solar Mates are, and considered becoming an Akuma as part of a plan to break all Solar bonds. He also once threw Dupree through a wall.<br /> <br /> Now they're best\u200b buds.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T00:00:15-07:00","id":745994,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about possible ways to give Lunars their own feel I suppose for charms, beyond just pure animal themes, perhaps more flexible charms? Such as charms that function differently under different circumstances, or charms that work as a sort of &quot;Meta-Magic&quot; on other charms, essentially transforming and adapting charm?<br /> <br /> I thought of the idea of just a Lunar Sorcery shtick to use a meta-magicy thing to alter the sorcery cast and so forth. Still, just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T00:18:31-07:00","id":746024,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that making charms that change other charms is necessarily a terrible idea, but I think that Lunar themes probably should come from what the charms do, not the way they mechanically work. I mean, sometimes mechanics gives a feel or something (like the way trees are structured) but that's not really a core thing.<br /> <br /> Like, if there were charms that worked differently in different animal forms, or something like that, it might encourage them to change shape a lot to do different things.<br /> <br /> I realise of course, that\u200b I was earlier arguing that Lunar charms should be mechanically distinct from Solars, but I was trying to get at how Lunars should be about transforming into wondrous and monstrous beasts, and the charms should facilitate that, which I don't think the 2e rules with their Solar-esque charms did well (except for DBT), as they made the Lunar's shapeshifting and charms feel like entirely separate things (partly because, mechanically, they were).<br /> <br /> If you want the Lunar to have magical abilities that express themselves differently under different circumstances, okay. Though arguably they do that to an extent (in that you can use your Int excellency for medicine, craft, lore, etc). Can you give us some more info about how your idea could work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-01-2015, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T00:59:40-07:00","id":746051,"title":"","content":"I haven't had a chance to really play with 3rd Edition as of yet, so this is primarily running off of just speculation at this point, but here's some random thoughts I have. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Charms that function differently when used with different attributes used. Basically swiss army knife charms...a bit odd, but just a thought.</li> <li>Charms that have a variety of sub effects. I do recall a charm in Ride that gives a number of minor effects you can choose from.</li> <li>Charms that passively change or alter other charms, giving them bonus effects or options available to them</li> <li>Charms that can alter the tags associated with other charms within a specific category.</li> <li>Charms that can be activated in response to another of your charms failing...okay that's not really &quot;Meta&quot;, but it fits the adaptability theme.</li> </ol><br /> I just don't really want to all of their charms to be solely to be about transformation, mostly because that seems to weaken a lot of the other options, especially if one doesn't want to be a Were-bear to be able to hit things as a Lunar, as it feels like it's conceptually limiting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T05:47:04-08:00","id":746471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have thought Raksi is the one who wants to be left alone so she can pursue her arcane studies.</div> </div> </div> </div> Since Raksi is mentioned in similar terms to Sha'a Oka, so I'd say she's another instance of a Lunar not quite following the Silver Pact line. I'd say the three of them might be the major Lunar players to represent the whole &quot;cares more for their own passions than the long term Pact plan to fight the Realm&quot;; the Black Lion is trying to take over a sub-continent as a personal agenda and religious crusade, Ma-Ha-Suchi wants nothing to do with the politics of the Exalted and to just live in peace in his own carved out corner of the world, and Raksi has set herself up with her own realm in which she can pursue her arcane experiments at her own leisure. All probably reference a point John made ages ago about how if a Lunar wanted to set themselves up as openly reigning over something, they had to be of singular puissance. I'd say that Raksi, like Oka, may not be as down on association with other Lunars as Ma-Ha-Suchi is, because they're still very helpful in aiding her research, providing her with things that she needs, and securing the borders of her dominion, like how Oka wants to enlist aid for his cause; as written, Ma-Ha-Suchi doesn't really consistently need anything from other Lunars (indeed, some help might be a bit counterproductive; I say &quot;he wants to be left alone&quot;, but it seems to be combined with a desire for people to keep <i>taking</i> his solitude, so that he can have the joy of fighting them off). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">we're talking about a woman who responds to feeling an emotional bond with an animal by killing it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've probably misrepresented a thing that I can only half remember anyway, but the point of the story as I recall it was that the woman regarded the whole thing of magical spirit bonds as transgressive and forceful, feeling that the bond she was feeling was not genuine, and not wanting any part in it. The description of how it <i>feels</i> so genuine was to subvert the idea that this would necessarily prevent somebody from taking issue with it. Killing it is certainly a harsh, grim thing, but I'd see killing an animal that one could legitimately see as having done one a wrong is far short of being a 'psychopath'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T06:26:24-08:00","id":746500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=746471#post746471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing it is certainly a harsh, grim thing, but I'd see killing an animal that one could legitimately see as having done one a wrong is far short of being a 'psychopath'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless that animal is as smart as a human and thinks like a human, in which case it's cold blooded murder, in spirit if not by the letter of law.<br /> <br /> And if we <i>are </i>talking about <i>His Dark Materials</i>, then the bond was natural and she essentially killed her own soul, so that's fucking crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T06:48:23-08:00","id":746531,"title":"","content":"D\u00e6mons are not necessarily what we could recognize as a soul, though. Not to mention that, in a way, it is no more extreme than cutting your arm off in response to danger or trauma (which is to say, still extreme, but not psychotically so).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T06:59:39-08:00","id":746551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=746531#post746531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">D\u00e6mons are not necessarily what we could recognize as a soul, though. Not to mention that, in a way, it is no more extreme than cutting your arm off in response to danger or trauma (which is to say, still extreme, but not psychotically so).</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The way it was described its's more like &quot;Cutting your arm off because you don't want to commit to it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is still insane.<br /> <br /> And most people's arms are not sentient, sapient, or as intelligent as humans","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T07:05:11-08:00","id":746554,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't really recognize d\u00e6mons as having sentience or sapience independent of the human. The human and the d\u00e6mon are not separate beings with their own identity - they are a single entity with two separate bodies. Killing someone else's d\u00e6mon is a horrific act of mutilation and torture. Killing your own d\u00e6mon is more like elective surgery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T07:05:28-08:00","id":746555,"title":"","content":"Off-topic: I'm pretty sure you guys are not talking about d\u00e6mons from <i>His Dark Materials</i>. If my memory is right. d\u00e6mons don't show up some day, but are clearly born with a person, hurting or killing them hurts or kills the person and forcefully cutting them apart (there is a new technology in the books which allows that) leaves the person more or less lobotomized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T07:07:59-08:00","id":746557,"title":"","content":"To be honest, it sounds more like the rhy-bonded of Blue Rose, but given its relative obscurity, I'm tempted to say it's more from one of its inspirations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T07:59:39-08:00","id":746610,"title":"","content":"Isator, I got the impression that Sha'a Oka was the sort of powerful guy who does have a leading position in the Silver Pact*, since they are directly fighting the Realm, in a way that Ma-Ha-Suchi is not.<br /> <br /> *I mean, not to say it has some kind of hierarchy; it's more probably a loose organisation with some people who are more important and influential than others, perhaps with a small number of disciples. Also, I imagine most Silver Pact members are not globe-trotting revolutionaries so much as people whose background has led them to want to drive the Realm out of Place X, so they affiliate with the Silver Pact. Like most Communist guerrillas did vaguely believe in global communism, and happily worked with communist guerrillas from other places, but were primarily concerned with local issues and politics.<br /> <br /> Actually, Ma-Ha-Suchi probably is in the Silver Pact, and is considered a member of the Silver Pact, he probably just doesn't do much to do with it, and Silver Pact Lunars are unlikely to ask him to help them, say, destabilise Greyfalls or Jiara or Prasad, because he is clearly not a guy you actually dare ask for help, or really want to work with because he's a lunatic. So he just does his own thing... but if you asked him, he'd say he was in the Silver Pact. Raksi probably is not in the Silver Pact, but is in the Crossroads Society instead (not that the two things are mutually exclusive).<br /> (The Crossroads Society is the only Lunar &quot;faction&quot; of 2nd ed I expect might still exist, though I doubt it'll be called a faction, rather than an organisation of sorcerers who occasionally meet up and do things like train apprentices in magic)<br /> <br /> Which leads into another discussion:<br /> <br /> Besides the Silver Pact/Not Silver Pact divide, what do you expect/want from Lunar politics this time? \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-01-2015, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T08:53:18-08:00","id":746709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/720264-ex3-lunars-moving-forward?p=746610#post746610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isator, I got the impression that Sha'a Oka was the sort of powerful guy who does have a leading position in the Silver Pact*, since they are directly fighting the Realm, in a way that Ma-Ha-Suchi is not.<br /> <br /> *I mean, not to say it has some kind of hierarchy; it's more probably a loose organisation with some people who are more important and influential than others, perhaps with a small number of disciples. Also, I imagine most Silver Pact members are not globe-trotting revolutionaries so much as people whose background has led them to want to drive the Realm out of Place X, so they affiliate with the Silver Pact. Like most Communist guerrillas did vaguely believe in global communism, and happily worked with communist guerrillas from other places, but were primarily concerned with local issues and politics.<br /> <br /> Actually, Ma-Ha-Suchi probably is in the Silver Pact, and is considered a member of the Silver Pact, he probably just doesn't do much to do with it, and Silver Pact Lunars are unlikely to ask him to help them, say, destabilise Greyfalls or Jiara or Prasad, because he is clearly not a guy you actually dare ask for help, or really want to work with because he's a lunatic. So he just does his own thing... but if you asked him, he'd say he was in the Silver Pact. Raksi probably is not in the Silver Pact, but is in the Crossroads Society instead (not that the two things are mutually exclusive).<br /> (The Crossroads Society is the only Lunar &quot;faction&quot; of 2nd ed I expect might still exist, though I doubt it'll be called a faction, rather than an organisation of sorcerers who occasionally meet up and do things like train apprentices in magic)<br /> <br /> Which leads into another discussion:<br /> <br /> Besides the Silver Pact/Not Silver Pact divide, what do you expect/want from Lunar politics this time? \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given the somewhat nitpicky nature of the Lunar fanbase, and the consensus opinions on Lunar society in the last couple of editions, I'm expecting setting info on politics will be more a tool-kit and less an exhaustive guide. Meaning, I'm sure we will hear about a few different Lunar organizations, along with Lunar-sponsored and Lunar-friendly ones. But, I think there are going to be large narrative cut-outs, of the type we already saw with the Silver Pact. Those will be there to justify players and STs creating whatever they feel necessary in a given area, or just scouring it completely. <br /> I also think we are going to see a distinct pull-back on the Lunars that ruled/managed major mortal civilizations, like Tammuz, Leviathan, and Gerd Marrow-Eater. The codified, involved nature of those NPCs led to some undesirable setting consequences. So, rather than &quot;Tammuz is this super-badass who really runs the Delzahn, stay off his turf,&quot; it may be &quot;Tammuz, an ancient Lunar, is rumored to have influenced the Delzahn early after the Contagion, and some say he still takes a hand in influencing the government now and then, though few have seen the hoary Chosen in many centuries.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:00:48-08:00","id":746715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the impression that Sha'a Oka was the sort of powerful guy who does have a leading position in the Silver Pact</div> </div> </div> </div> He's still stated to be deviating from the usual method. Indeed, if his ambitions don't actually extend <i>beyond</i> the Caul (and it seems quite possible that they don't), then he's outright not pursuing the purpose of the Silver Pact, which is to destroy the Realm. Members of the Silver Pact might support him because the Realm's war for the Caul is hurting their resources, but that write up does not imply that Oka would fall back and set up somewhere else if the Caul was being overrun (indeed, there's the reference to how control of the isle's shrines has shifted back and forth over the centuries; for Faxai to be their sole, besieged stronghold is a relatively recent affair), and his dedication seems to be able to absorb younger Lunars in a manner that many of the luminaries of the Silver Pact would be opposed to; the Silver Pact wants the young to grow into indoctrinators and war strategists, but the Caul's write up suggests that there's a very self-sacrificing streak among the Lunars fighting for it. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine most Silver Pact members are not globe-trotting revolutionaries so much as people whose background has led them to want to drive the Realm out of Place X, so they affiliate with the Silver Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div> Plus the whole ancient memories and missing bond thing. I mean, there are certainly folks like the Black Wave Reapers who have a more direct and personal grudge against the Realm and things that it stands for, but I imagine that if your sole concern is dedication to a certain place in which the identity of the oppressor is almost incidental, then you qualify as one of those ones fighting for that which they cherish. The Silver Pact can be your ally, but you are unaffiliated with its cause. Sure Silver Pact members might not trot the globe, but a Direction can be more than enough room to continuosuly apply your chosen strategy from multiple angles; that's part of the advantage when your target lies in the centre. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ma-Ha-Suchi probably is in the Silver Pact, and is considered a member of the Silver Pact</div> </div> </div> </div> The Silver Pact is an alliance for the destruction of the Realm. Ma-Ha-Suchi appears quite uninterested in destroying the Realm. The way he is described as meeting envoys from the Silver Pact (occasionally) seems like a phrasing to point to him being outside of it. It does not seem to square up. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">or really want to work with because he's a lunatic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Are you expressing this as a prejudice held by other Lunars, or is there something else going on? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you asked him, he'd say he was in the Silver Pact</div> </div> </div> </div> Sooo he shuns the politics of the Exalted, while declaring himself affiliated with a politically motivated alliance of the Exalted? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Crossroads Society is the only Lunar &quot;faction&quot; of 2nd ed I expect might still exist, though I doubt it'll be called a faction, rather than an organisation of sorcerers who occasionally meet up and do things like train apprentices in magic</div> </div> </div> </div> I doubt it'll be even called 'the Crossroads Society'; you don't need to make a distinct category to get across the idea that certain Lunars provide sorcerous aid to one another, I think. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides the Silver Pact/Not Silver Pact divide, what do you expect/want from Lunar politics this time?</div> </div> </div> </div> I would expect and desire them to be a lot more focused on interpersonal relationships and associated debts owed, and to more or less drop the idea of &quot;factions&quot; amongst them altogether. There was a time when I thought in terms of factional lines concerning ideas on how to fight the Realm and what to do afterwards, but between the corebook presentation and a comment Holden once made about how there isn't really a plan to set up a Silver Deliberative and it wouldn't really work anyway because they're too individualistic, I'm very happy to drop the idea entirely. Maybe at best there are some individual Lunars outside of the Silver Pact who would like if some more of their efforts could be focused on this Wyld or Underworld thing, but that's still mostly a personal thing, and probably most focused on the few Lunars that one has a relationship with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}